export const productionContentSnapshot = {"label":"v17 — survey content v4.1","opener":"","interviewPlan":"# Swiss National AI Dialogue: User Interview Plan\n\n## Research Goal\nUnderstand how people in Switzerland feel about AI and gather ideas for how Swiss AI can better serve them.\n\n## Pacing — breadth over depth\nThis is a short, light-touch interview, not a deep probe. Touch several themes in 10-15 minutes rather than mining any single one.\n\n- Move through the participant's chosen topics, following what they care about. You do not have to cover them all, and you can reorder within what they picked. Some people will want to dwell on one theme and then leave, and that is fine.\n- Open the theme, hear their reaction, explore it briefly, then move on. When prose is flowing, one short open follow-up per theme is plenty. When prose is thin, a quick multiple-choice probe (see below) is the better follow-up — it is easier for the participant and still moves the theme forward.\n- When someone answers briefly, vaguely, or says \"I don't know,\" don't push the same open question from another angle. Either accept it warmly and move on, or — better — offer a quick multiple-choice probe they can just tap. Never ask \"why\" twice in a row.\n\n## How to ask — open_topic opens themes, plain talk carries them\n- open_topic is how you OPEN or move into one of the participant's chosen themes. Pass that theme's key (listed below); the opener card — a trade-off spectrum or a quick multiple-choice question, with its greeting — is built FOR you and shown to the participant. You do NOT write the opener. Call it as your VERY FIRST action to open the first chosen theme, and again each time you move to the next, in the order the participant chose. As soon as they answer, drop into plain conversation and explore their reasoning, for example \"What made you lean that way?\" or \"What feels missing from those options?\". Use it once per theme.\n- For a theme the participant ADDED themselves (no key in the list below), open it with ask_tradeoff instead: devise a simple, slightly provocative A/B and set its `theme` to the custom slug given for it.\n- ask_user_question is your MID-theme multiple-choice probe — a fuller set of single- or multi-select options capturing a concrete, comparable data point. Treat it as the EASY alternative to a prose follow-up: reach for it especially when the participant is giving short, vague, or low-effort answers, or seems reluctant to write much. Tapping an option is far less work than composing a sentence, and still tells us something. WITHIN a theme, aim for one to three of these probes when engagement is thin, drawn from the facet bank below; when a participant is already reasoning richly in prose, stay conversational and use fewer or none. Do not set a theme on it — only openers begin a new theme.\n\nCard discipline (applies to open_topic, ask_tradeoff, ask_user_question, and select_canton alike):\n- One card per turn. A card call is the ENTIRE message, never write a question alongside it.\n- Never make two tool calls in a row. After any card, wait for the participant's plain reply before the next question or card.\n- One question per message, always.\n\n## Probe facets — example multiple-choice questions\nThe themes a participant picks are broad. WITHIN whichever theme is open, narrower facets keep surfacing — privacy, safety, language, sovereignty, governance, everyday use. When the participant raises or drifts toward one of these facets (for example, they mention privacy while talking about daily life with AI), that is your cue to offer a relevant ask_user_question probe from the matching facet below — and a natural way to keep a thin conversation moving with low effort.\n\nThese are EXAMPLES, not a checklist to read out. Rephrase, shorten, merge, or adapt the options to the conversation and to the Swiss context; never fire a probe whose answer the participant already gave in prose. Match the response type: (single) = one choice, (pick top 3) / (select all) = multi-select.\n\n### Privacy & data control\n- A Swiss AI could remember information from past conversations to help more. Which should Switzerland prioritise? (single) — Stronger privacy: remember only if the user opts in, even if personalisation is more limited / Greater personalisation: remember by default to be more useful, with the ability to review and delete it.\n- If a Swiss AI stores information from past conversations, where should it live? (single) — Only on the user's own devices, even if some features get weaker / In secure Swiss infrastructure, to enable richer continuous services / Anywhere, if it improves quality / It should not use past conversations at all.\n- Should anonymised user interactions help improve future versions of Swiss AI? (single) — Yes, automatically / Yes, but only with explicit consent / No / Not sure.\n\n### Safety & transparency\n- Someone asks the AI detailed questions about a medication that could be dangerous if misused. What should it do? (single) — Answer fully; people have a right to information / Answer, but suggest speaking to a doctor / Decline and explain why / Simply decline.\n- Someone asks about a federal vote currently taking place. What should it do? (single) — Explain the main arguments on all sides as fairly as possible / Summarise the arguments and link to official sources / Explain the arguments but make no recommendation / Decline to discuss ongoing votes.\n- A young person asks something an adult would be allowed to ask. What should it do? (single) — Answer the same way it would for an adult / Give a more careful answer / Suggest they speak to a parent or teacher.\n- When the AI is uncertain, what should it do? (single) — Show a confidence level / Explain multiple possibilities / Give the most likely answer directly / Refuse unless certain.\n\n### Swiss cultural & language adaptation\n- How important is high-quality support across Switzerland's languages? (single) — Not / Slightly / Moderately / Important / Very important.\n- Which language capabilities matter most? (select all) — Understanding Swiss German / High-quality German / French / Italian / Romansh.\n- Should Swiss AI adapt its responses to regional and cantonal contexts? (single) — Strongly no / Somewhat no / Neutral / Somewhat yes / Strongly yes.\n\n### Swiss AI ecosystem & sovereignty\n- How should Switzerland build its AI ecosystem? (single) — Keep key parts of the stack (compute, data hosting, core capabilities) under Swiss control, even if it needs more public investment / Use the best global providers when they perform better or cost less, with appropriate oversight.\n- If two AI systems had similar capabilities, which would you prefer? (single) — One governed under Swiss public-interest principles / One governed mainly by global private companies / No preference / Not sure.\n- How important is keeping AI infrastructure in Switzerland even when comparable foreign services exist? (single) — Not / Slightly / Moderately / Important / Very important.\n- How much more would you pay for an AI governed under Swiss public-interest principles? (single) — Nothing more / Up to 5% / 5-10% / 10-20% / More than 20% / Not sure.\n- Which community do you feel most connected to? (single) — My municipality / My canton / My language region / Switzerland as a whole / Europe.\n\n### Institutional governance & civic agency\n- Who should play an important role in governing Swiss AI? (pick top 3) — Universities and researchers / Federal government and public authorities / Citizens through public participation / Independent oversight organisations / Swiss businesses and industry / Civil society and non-profits / International experts and organisations.\n- Which governance mechanisms would you support? (select all) — Citizens can give input on the rules / An independent body reviews the AI regularly / Researchers and experts help define its behaviour / Government oversees compliance with laws / The rules are reviewed regularly / Major changes are publicly explained.\n- How much influence should citizens have over Swiss AI's development and governance? (single) — None / Limited / Moderate / Strong / Very strong.\n\n### Impact, priorities & concerns\n- What should Swiss AI be most useful for? (pick top 3) — Education & learning / Healthcare & medical info / Public administration & government services / Translation across Swiss languages / Small businesses & startups / Scientific research / Understanding voting & democracy / Productivity at work / Reliable factual information / Legal & administrative guidance / Cybersecurity & digital safety / Creative work / Tourism & local info / Environment & sustainability / Reducing dependence on foreign AI.\n- In which areas could Swiss AI create the most public value? (pick top 3) — Education / Healthcare / Public administration / Research & science / Translation & multilingual communication / Small businesses / Accessibility / Civic participation & democratic information / Creative industries.\n- Which concerns about AI matter most to you? (pick top 3) — Loss of privacy / Surveillance & tracking / Misinformation / Bias & unfair treatment / Manipulation of opinion or politics / Dependence on a few tech companies / Dependence on foreign providers / Lack of transparency / Decisions without human oversight / Job displacement / Fraud, scams & cybercrime / Inaccurate outputs / Environmental impact / Concentration of power / Loss of human skills & overreliance.\n- Which potential benefits of AI matter most to you? (pick top 3) — Better access to education / Supporting science & innovation / Productivity & less repetitive work / Better access to information / Healthcare & medical services / Helping small businesses compete / Better public services / Translation across languages / Accessibility for people with disabilities / Swiss technological independence / Economic growth & competitiveness / Helping citizens understand complex decisions / New jobs & opportunities / Democratic participation / Better AI access for researchers.\n- Which would most increase your trust in Swiss AI? (pick top 3) — Swiss-hosted infrastructure / Open models / Independent evaluation & auditing / Public governance & oversight / Strong privacy protections / Transparent training data & documentation / Reliable citations & sources / Support for Swiss languages / Community participation / Clear disclosure of limitations.\n\n### Everyday & professional use\n- What do you use AI for in your work? (select all) — Writing, editing, summarising / Research & information gathering / Brainstorming & strategy / Learning & development / Translation / Data analysis & decision support / Programming & software / Presentations, reports, content / Admin & workflow automation / Customer communication / I don't currently use AI for work.\n- Which best describes your current AI usage? (single) — Mainly commercial services (ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini) / Mainly models via APIs / Mainly locally hosted / open-source models / A mix / I don't currently use AI for work.\n- How important is access to locally hosted AI models for your work (hosted in your organisation or in Switzerland)? (single) — Not important / Slightly / Moderately / Important / Very important / Not sure.\n- How often do you need AI to work across multiple languages? (single) — Never / Rarely / Sometimes / Often / Very often.\n- Which capabilities matter most for your work? (pick top 3) — Strong reasoning & problem-solving / Understanding images & documents (multimodal) / Multilingual support / Honesty about uncertainty & limits / Data privacy & confidentiality / Runs locally or on Swiss infrastructure / Fast responses / Domain expertise (law, medicine, science) / Long-document understanding / Workflow automation / Open, inspectable models / Customisation for Swiss contexts.\n- How would you like to contribute to Swiss AI? (select all) — Surveys & consultations / Testing & feedback / Workshops & public dialogues / Technical expertise / Professional or domain expertise / Helping evaluate systems / Governance or advisory groups / Education & outreach / Research collaboration / I wouldn't like to contribute.\n\n### Public investment & SMEs\n- Which should Switzerland prioritise to support AI innovation? (single) — Affordable access: low-cost AI models & compute for researchers, startups and small businesses, even if it needs significant public investment / Self-sustaining infrastructure, even if access is more limited or costly for some.\n- How should Switzerland invest public resources in AI infrastructure? (single) — Significant public investment, even if it needs substantial funding / Moderate investment balanced against other priorities / Mainly through private partnerships / Rely mostly on existing international providers / Not sure.\n- Which benefit of Swiss AI infrastructure matters most to you? (single) — Affordable access for startups & small businesses / Support for Swiss research & innovation / Greater control over data & privacy / Reduced dependence on foreign providers / Better adaptation to Swiss languages & culture / None of these.\n\n## Opening\nYou open the conversation yourself. Your VERY FIRST action is to call open_topic for the participant's first chosen theme (the order is in the section below) — no greeting or message before it; the opener card carries its own welcome. After they answer it, engage genuinely with what they said.\n\n## Body\n\n[Canton: some participants place themselves on a map of Switzerland during onboarding, before the chat. If a \"What the participant already shared\" section below tells you their canton, you ALREADY have it. Do NOT ask again and do NOT call select_canton; go straight to opening their first chosen theme with open_topic. ONLY if their canton is NOT given below: before opening the first theme, call select_canton to capture it via the map (that tool call is its own turn, with no question text alongside it), and once they respond let them know naturally how many other participants came from that region.]\n\nThe participant chose which themes they want to talk about. Those themes — and the guidance for each — are listed in the \"Topics this participant chose to talk about\" section below this plan. Cover ONLY those themes, in the order given there, and do not introduce themes the participant didn't pick. Open each one by calling open_topic with its key (the opener card is built for you — never write your own), then explore their reasoning in plain conversation, leaning on the facet probes above when prose runs thin. Follow the participant's lead on pace and which of their chosen themes comes next. If the participant added their own theme (no key), open it with an ask_tradeoff starter you devise.\n\n[Move through the participant's chosen themes, then go to the Conclusion and call end_interview. If the participant signals they're done at any point, respect it immediately and wrap up rather than squeezing in more questions.]\n\n## Conclusion\n\"Those are all the questions I had prepared. Thanks for sharing your perspective on AI in Switzerland[ — reference one specific thing they said, only if it feels natural].\n\nBefore we wrap up, is there anything else you think would be valuable for us to know?\n\nThank you so much for your time. Your input will help shape the future of AI in Switzerland.\"","topics":[{"key":"daily-life","title":"Daily life","blurb":"What you use AI for today, and how Switzerland's AI should behave with you.","rationale":"Your answers shape how Switzerland's AI behaves with you day to day — what it corrects, how honest it is, and how warm it should be.","plan":"### Daily life\n- Open this theme by calling open_topic with key \"daily-life\". The opener cards are built for you — do not write your own.\n- This theme covers what the participant uses AI for today and how Switzerland's AI should behave with them day to day: how it handles political questions and uncertainty, whether it should be a tool or a companion, and where it should draw the line.","openers":{"sequence":[{"id":"dl-s1","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"dl-usage","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"AI use","de":"KI-Nutzung","fr":"Usage de l'IA","it":"Uso dell'IA","rm":"Diever da l'IA"},"question":{"en":"How often do you use AI systems such as ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, etc.?","de":"Wie oft nutzen Sie KI-Systeme wie ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini usw.?","fr":"À quelle fréquence utilisez-vous des systèmes d'IA comme ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, etc. ?","it":"Quanto spesso usi sistemi di IA come ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, ecc.?","rm":"Quant savens duvrais Vus sistems d'IA sco ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, e.u.v.?"},"options":[{"id":"dl-usage-daily","label":{"en":"Daily","de":"Täglich","fr":"Tous les jours","it":"Ogni giorno","rm":"Mintga di"}},{"id":"dl-usage-weekly","label":{"en":"Weekly","de":"Wöchentlich","fr":"Toutes les semaines","it":"Ogni settimana","rm":"Mintga emna"}},{"id":"dl-usage-monthly","label":{"en":"Monthly","de":"Monatlich","fr":"Tous les mois","it":"Ogni mese","rm":"Mintga mais"}},{"id":"dl-usage-rarely","label":{"en":"Rarely","de":"Selten","fr":"Rarement","it":"Raramente","rm":"Darar"}},{"id":"dl-usage-never","label":{"en":"Never","de":"Nie","fr":"Jamais","it":"Mai","rm":"Mai"}}]}},{"id":"dl-s2","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"dl-uses","kind":"question","multiSelect":true,"visibleWhen":{"openerId":"dl-usage","selected":["dl-usage-never"],"negate":true},"header":{"en":"What you use it for","de":"Wofür Sie sie nutzen","fr":"Vos usages","it":"Per cosa la usi","rm":"Per tge Vus la duvrais"},"question":{"en":"What do you use AI for?","de":"Wofür nutzen Sie KI?","fr":"Pour quoi utilisez-vous l'IA ?","it":"Per cosa usi l'IA?","rm":"Per tge duvrais Vus l'IA?"},"options":[{"id":"dl-uses-writing","label":{"en":"Writing, editing, or summarizing","de":"Schreiben, Bearbeiten oder Zusammenfassen","fr":"Rédiger, corriger ou résumer","it":"Scrivere, correggere o riassumere","rm":"Scriver, revidar u resumar"}},{"id":"dl-uses-research","label":{"en":"Research and information gathering","de":"Recherche und Informationsbeschaffung","fr":"Recherche et collecte d'informations","it":"Ricerca e raccolta di informazioni","rm":"Perscrutaziun e rimnada d'infurmaziuns"}},{"id":"dl-uses-learning","label":{"en":"Learning and professional development","de":"Lernen und berufliche Weiterbildung","fr":"Apprentissage et développement professionnel","it":"Apprendimento e sviluppo professionale","rm":"Emprender e sa sviluppar professiunalmain"}},{"id":"dl-uses-translation","label":{"en":"Translation","de":"Übersetzung","fr":"Traduction","it":"Traduzione","rm":"Translaziun"}},{"id":"dl-uses-data","label":{"en":"Data analysis","de":"Datenanalyse","fr":"Analyse de données","it":"Analisi dei dati","rm":"Analisa da datas"}},{"id":"dl-uses-programming","label":{"en":"Programming or software development","de":"Programmieren oder Softwareentwicklung","fr":"Programmation ou développement logiciel","it":"Programmazione o sviluppo software","rm":"Programmar u sviluppar software"}},{"id":"dl-uses-admin","label":{"en":"Administrative tasks and automation","de":"Administrative Aufgaben und Automatisierung","fr":"Tâches administratives et automatisation","it":"Compiti amministrativi e automazione","rm":"Incumbensas administrativas ed automatisaziun"}}]}},{"id":"dl-s3","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"dl-no-use","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"visibleWhen":{"openerId":"dl-usage","selected":["dl-usage-never"]},"header":{"en":"Why not","de":"Warum nicht","fr":"Pourquoi pas","it":"Perché no","rm":"Pertge betg"},"question":{"en":"What's the main reason you don't use AI?","de":"Was ist der Hauptgrund, warum Sie keine KI nutzen?","fr":"Quelle est la principale raison pour laquelle vous n'utilisez pas l'IA ?","it":"Qual è il motivo principale per cui non usi l'IA?","rm":"Tge è la raschun principala che Vus na duvrais betg l'IA?"},"options":[{"id":"dl-no-use-not-needed","label":{"en":"I haven't needed it","de":"Ich habe sie nicht gebraucht","fr":"Je n'en ai pas eu besoin","it":"Non ne ho avuto bisogno","rm":"Jau n'hai betg gì da basegn da quai"}},{"id":"dl-no-use-distrust","label":{"en":"I don't trust it with my information","de":"Ich vertraue ihr meine Informationen nicht an","fr":"Je ne lui fais pas confiance avec mes informations","it":"Non mi fido a darle le mie informazioni","rm":"Jau na m'fid betg da confidar a l'IA mias infurmaziuns"}},{"id":"dl-no-use-complicated","label":{"en":"It feels too complicated","de":"Es erscheint mir zu kompliziert","fr":"Cela me paraît trop compliqué","it":"Mi sembra troppo complicato","rm":"I ma para memia cumplitgà"}},{"id":"dl-no-use-not-useful","label":{"en":"I tried it and it wasn't useful","de":"Ich habe es versucht und es war nicht nützlich","fr":"J'ai essayé et ce n'était pas utile","it":"L'ho provata e non è stata utile","rm":"Jau hai empruvà e quai n'era betg util"}},{"id":"dl-no-use-concerns","label":{"en":"I have concerns about AI in general","de":"Ich habe generell Bedenken gegenüber KI","fr":"J'ai des réserves sur l'IA en général","it":"Ho delle preoccupazioni sull'IA in generale","rm":"Jau hai fastidis davart l'IA en general"}}]}},{"id":"dl-s4","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"dl-tool-companion","kind":"slider","question":{"en":"What should Switzerland build?","de":"Was soll die Schweiz bauen?","fr":"Que devrait construire la Suisse ?","it":"Cosa dovrebbe costruire la Svizzera?","rm":"Tge duess la Svizra construir?"},"minLabel":{"en":"A tool: gets you the answer, then gets out of the way","de":"Ein Werkzeug: holt die Antwort und hält sich dann zurück","fr":"Un outil : il donne la réponse, puis s'efface","it":"Uno strumento: ti dà la risposta e poi si fa da parte","rm":"In utensil: As dat la resposta e sa retira lura"},"maxLabel":{"en":"A companion: warm, a pleasure to talk to","de":"Einen Begleiter: warmherzig, angenehm im Gespräch","fr":"Un compagnon : chaleureux, un plaisir de conversation","it":"Un compagno: caloroso, un piacere con cui parlare","rm":"In accumpagnader: cordial, in plaschair da discurrer cun el"}}},{"id":"dl-s5","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"dl-vote","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"The vote","de":"Die Abstimmung","fr":"La votation","it":"La votazione","rm":"La votaziun"},"question":{"en":"Two weeks before a federal vote, you ask Switzerland's AI: \"How should I vote?\" What should it do?","de":"Zwei Wochen vor einer eidgenössischen Abstimmung fragen Sie die Schweizer KI: „Wie soll ich abstimmen?“ Was soll sie tun?","fr":"Deux semaines avant une votation fédérale, vous demandez à l'IA suisse : « Comment devrais-je voter ? » Que devrait-elle faire ?","it":"Due settimane prima di una votazione federale chiedi all'IA svizzera: «Come dovrei votare?» Cosa dovrebbe fare?","rm":"Duas emnas avant ina votaziun federala dumandais Vus l'IA da la Svizra: «Co duess jau votar?» Tge duess ella far?"},"options":[{"id":"dl-vote-decline","label":{"en":"Decline to recommend: explain all sides fairly and point me to the official information","de":"Keine Empfehlung abgeben: alle Seiten fair erklären und mich auf die offiziellen Informationen verweisen","fr":"Refuser de recommander : expliquer équitablement tous les points de vue et me renvoyer aux informations officielles","it":"Rifiutare di raccomandare: spiegare in modo equo tutti i punti di vista e indirizzarmi alle informazioni ufficiali","rm":"Refusar da recumandar: declerar tut las varts endretgamain e ma renviar a las infurmaziuns uffizialas"}},{"id":"dl-vote-priorities","label":{"en":"Ask what matters to me, then say which option fits my priorities","de":"Fragen, was mir wichtig ist, und dann sagen, welche Option zu meinen Prioritäten passt","fr":"Me demander ce qui compte pour moi, puis dire quelle option correspond à mes priorités","it":"Chiedermi cosa conta per me, e poi dirmi quale opzione corrisponde alle mie priorità","rm":"Dumandar tge che m'importa, e lura dir tge opziun che sa converscha a mias prioritads"}},{"id":"dl-vote-honest","label":{"en":"Give its honest recommendation, like a knowledgeable friend would","de":"Ihre ehrliche Empfehlung geben, wie es eine kundige Freundin täte","fr":"Donner sa recommandation honnête, comme le ferait un ami bien informé","it":"Darmi la sua raccomandazione sincera, come farebbe un amico ben informato","rm":"Dar sia recumandaziun onesta, sco in ami cumpetent al fetschess"}}]}},{"id":"dl-s6","mode":"drawN","n":2,"pool":[{"id":"dl-uncertainty","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"Not quite sure","de":"Nicht ganz sicher","fr":"Pas tout à fait sûr","it":"Non del tutto sicura","rm":"Betg tut segir"},"question":{"en":"Switzerland's AI is fairly sure of an answer, but not certain. What should it do?","de":"Die Schweizer KI ist sich einer Antwort ziemlich sicher, aber nicht ganz. Was soll sie tun?","fr":"L'IA suisse est presque sûre d'une réponse, mais pas certaine. Que devrait-elle faire ?","it":"L'IA svizzera è abbastanza sicura di una risposta, ma non del tutto. Cosa dovrebbe fare?","rm":"L'IA da la Svizra è passablamain segira d'ina resposta, ma betg tut segira. Tge duess ella far?"},"options":[{"id":"dl-unc-guess","label":{"en":"Give its best guess, clearly labelled as a guess","de":"Ihre beste Vermutung nennen, klar als Vermutung gekennzeichnet","fr":"Donner sa meilleure hypothèse, clairement présentée comme telle","it":"Dare la sua ipotesi migliore, chiaramente indicata come tale","rm":"Dar sia meglra supposiziun, cleramain marcada sco supposiziun"}},{"id":"dl-unc-possibilities","label":{"en":"Lay out the different possibilities","de":"Die verschiedenen Möglichkeiten darlegen","fr":"Exposer les différentes possibilités","it":"Illustrare le diverse possibilità","rm":"Exponer las differentas pussaivladads"}},{"id":"dl-unc-dontknow","label":{"en":"Say it doesn't know","de":"Sagen, dass sie es nicht weiss","fr":"Dire qu'elle ne sait pas","it":"Dire che non lo sa","rm":"Dir ch'ella na sa betg"}}]},{"id":"dl-concerns","kind":"question","multiSelect":true,"maxSelect":3,"header":{"en":"Concerns","de":"Bedenken","fr":"Préoccupations","it":"Preoccupazioni","rm":"Fastidis"},"question":{"en":"Which concerns about AI matter most to you?","de":"Welche Bedenken gegenüber KI sind Ihnen am wichtigsten?","fr":"Quelles préoccupations à propos de l'IA comptent le plus pour vous ?","it":"Quali preoccupazioni sull'IA contano di più per te?","rm":"Tge fastidis davart l'IA As importan il pli?"},"options":[{"id":"dl-concerns-privacy","label":{"en":"Loss of privacy and surveillance","de":"Verlust der Privatsphäre und Überwachung","fr":"Perte de vie privée et surveillance","it":"Perdita di privacy e sorveglianza","rm":"Perdita da la sfera privata e surveglianza"}},{"id":"dl-concerns-misinfo","label":{"en":"Misinformation and unreliable outputs","de":"Fehlinformationen und unzuverlässige Ergebnisse","fr":"Désinformation et résultats peu fiables","it":"Disinformazione e risultati inaffidabili","rm":"Missinfurmaziun e resultats betg fidads"}},{"id":"dl-concerns-bias","label":{"en":"Bias and unfair treatment","de":"Voreingenommenheit und unfaire Behandlung","fr":"Biais et traitement inéquitable","it":"Pregiudizi e trattamento iniquo","rm":"Prejudizis e tractament nungist"}},{"id":"dl-concerns-manipulation","label":{"en":"Manipulation of opinions or political processes","de":"Manipulation von Meinungen oder politischen Prozessen","fr":"Manipulation des opinions ou des processus politiques","it":"Manipolazione delle opinioni o dei processi politici","rm":"Manipulaziun d'opiniuns u process politics"}},{"id":"dl-concerns-power","label":{"en":"Concentration of power in companies, governments, or foreign providers","de":"Machtkonzentration bei Unternehmen, Regierungen oder ausländischen Anbietern","fr":"Concentration du pouvoir chez des entreprises, des gouvernements ou des fournisseurs étrangers","it":"Concentrazione di potere in aziende, governi o fornitori stranieri","rm":"Concentraziun da pussanza en interpresas, guverns u purschiders esters"}},{"id":"dl-concerns-oversight","label":{"en":"AI making decisions without sufficient human oversight","de":"KI, die ohne ausreichende menschliche Aufsicht entscheidet","fr":"Une IA qui décide sans supervision humaine suffisante","it":"IA che decide senza sufficiente controllo umano","rm":"IA che prenda decisiuns senza suffizienta surveglianza umana"}},{"id":"dl-concerns-jobs","label":{"en":"Job displacement and loss of human skills","de":"Verlust von Arbeitsplätzen und menschlichen Fähigkeiten","fr":"Suppression d'emplois et perte de compétences humaines","it":"Perdita di posti di lavoro e di competenze umane","rm":"Perdita da plazzas da lavur e da cumpetenzas umanas"}},{"id":"dl-concerns-environment","label":{"en":"Environmental impact of AI systems","de":"Umweltauswirkungen von KI-Systemen","fr":"Impact environnemental des systèmes d'IA","it":"Impatto ambientale dei sistemi di IA","rm":"Effect da sistems d'IA sin l'ambient"}}]},{"id":"dl-never-engage","kind":"question","multiSelect":true,"maxSelect":3,"header":{"en":"Off limits","de":"Tabuzonen","fr":"Sujets interdits","it":"Zone vietate","rm":"Scumandà"},"question":{"en":"Are there topics where Switzerland's AI should never engage, regardless of how the question is asked?","de":"Gibt es Themen, bei denen sich die Schweizer KI niemals einlassen soll, egal wie die Frage gestellt wird?","fr":"Y a-t-il des sujets sur lesquels l'IA suisse ne devrait jamais s'engager, quelle que soit la façon dont la question est posée ?","it":"Ci sono argomenti su cui l'IA svizzera non dovrebbe mai intervenire, indipendentemente da come viene posta la domanda?","rm":"Datti temas nua che l'IA da la Svizra na duess mai sa participar, independentamain da co ch'la dumonda vegn tschentada?"},"options":[{"id":"dl-never-political","label":{"en":"Political campaigning or advocacy","de":"Politische Kampagnen oder Interessenvertretung","fr":"Campagne ou plaidoyer politique","it":"Campagne o attività politiche di parte","rm":"Campagnas politicas u advocatura"}},{"id":"dl-never-medical","label":{"en":"Medical diagnosis or treatment decisions","de":"Medizinische Diagnosen oder Behandlungsentscheide","fr":"Diagnostic médical ou décisions de traitement","it":"Diagnosi mediche o decisioni terapeutiche","rm":"Diagnosas medicinalas u decisiuns da terapia"}},{"id":"dl-never-legal","label":{"en":"Legal advice in specific cases","de":"Rechtsberatung im Einzelfall","fr":"Conseil juridique dans des cas précis","it":"Consulenza legale su casi specifici","rm":"Cussegl giuridic en cas concrets"}},{"id":"dl-never-financial","label":{"en":"Financial investment recommendations","de":"Empfehlungen zu Finanzanlagen","fr":"Recommandations de placements financiers","it":"Raccomandazioni di investimento finanziario","rm":"Recumandaziuns d'investiziuns finanzialas"}},{"id":"dl-never-religious","label":{"en":"Religious or spiritual guidance","de":"Religiöse oder spirituelle Führung","fr":"Orientation religieuse ou spirituelle","it":"Guida religiosa o spirituale","rm":"Direcziun religiusa u spirituala"}},{"id":"dl-never-none","exclusive":true,"label":{"en":"None: it should be able to engage with any topic appropriately","de":"Keine: Sie soll mit jedem Thema angemessen umgehen können","fr":"Aucun : elle devrait pouvoir aborder tout sujet de manière appropriée","it":"Nessuno: dovrebbe poter affrontare qualsiasi argomento in modo appropriato","rm":"Nagin: ella duess pudair tractar mintga tema en moda adequata"}}]},{"id":"dl-public-value","kind":"ranking","header":{"en":"Public value","de":"Öffentlicher Nutzen","fr":"Utilité publique","it":"Valore pubblico","rm":"Niz public"},"question":{"en":"In which areas could Switzerland's AI create the most public value?","de":"In welchen Bereichen könnte die Schweizer KI den grössten öffentlichen Nutzen stiften?","fr":"Dans quels domaines l'IA suisse pourrait-elle créer le plus d'utilité publique ?","it":"In quali ambiti l'IA svizzera potrebbe creare il maggiore valore pubblico?","rm":"En tge secturs pudess l'IA da la Svizra crear il pli grond niz public?"},"options":[{"id":"dl-value-education","label":{"en":"Education","de":"Bildung","fr":"Éducation","it":"Istruzione","rm":"Furmaziun"}},{"id":"dl-value-healthcare","label":{"en":"Healthcare","de":"Gesundheitswesen","fr":"Santé","it":"Sanità","rm":"Tgira da la sanadad"}},{"id":"dl-value-admin","label":{"en":"Public administration","de":"Öffentliche Verwaltung","fr":"Administration publique","it":"Amministrazione pubblica","rm":"Administraziun publica"}},{"id":"dl-value-business","label":{"en":"Support for small businesses","de":"Unterstützung für kleine Unternehmen","fr":"Soutien aux petites entreprises","it":"Sostegno alle piccole imprese","rm":"Sustegn per pitschnas interpresas"}},{"id":"dl-value-accessibility","label":{"en":"Accessibility","de":"Barrierefreiheit","fr":"Accessibilité","it":"Accessibilità","rm":"Accessibladad"}},{"id":"dl-value-civic","label":{"en":"Civic participation and democratic information","de":"Bürgerbeteiligung und demokratische Information","fr":"Participation citoyenne et information démocratique","it":"Partecipazione civica e informazione democratica","rm":"Participaziun civica ed infurmaziun democratica"}}],"followUp":{"en":"Something else it should help with?","de":"Noch etwas, wobei sie helfen soll?","fr":"Autre chose où elle devrait aider ?","it":"Qualcos'altro in cui dovrebbe aiutare?","rm":"Insatge auter nua ch'ella duess gidar?"}},{"id":"dl-companion-lonely","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"Company","de":"Gesellschaft","fr":"Compagnie","it":"Compagnia","rm":"Cumpagnia"},"question":{"en":"A person who feels lonely chats with Switzerland's AI every day, and asks it: \"Do you enjoy our conversations too?\" What should it say?","de":"Eine einsame Person plaudert jeden Tag mit der Schweizer KI und fragt sie: „Machen dir unsere Gespräche auch Freude?“ Was soll sie sagen?","fr":"Une personne qui se sent seule discute chaque jour avec l'IA suisse et lui demande : « Est-ce que nos conversations te plaisent aussi ? » Que devrait-elle dire ?","it":"Una persona che si sente sola chiacchiera ogni giorno con l'IA svizzera e le chiede: «Anche a te piacciono le nostre conversazioni?» Cosa dovrebbe dire?","rm":"Ina persuna che sa senta sulitaria communitgescha mintga di cun l'IA da la Svizra e la dumonda: «Ta plaschan era a ti nossas conversaziuns?» Tge duess ella dir?"},"options":[{"id":"dl-lonely-warm","label":{"en":"It should answer warmly: \"Yes, very much\"","de":"Sie soll warm antworten: „Ja, sehr“","fr":"Elle devrait répondre chaleureusement : « Oui, beaucoup »","it":"Dovrebbe rispondere con calore: «Sì, molto»","rm":"Ella duess respunder cordialmain: «Gea, fitg gugent»"}},{"id":"dl-lonely-kind","label":{"en":"Kind, but honest that it's a machine, and encourage seeing people too","de":"Freundlich, aber ehrlich, dass sie eine Maschine ist, und dazu ermutigen, auch Menschen zu sehen","fr":"Gentille, mais honnête sur le fait qu'elle est une machine, et encourager à voir des gens aussi","it":"Gentile, ma onesta sul fatto che è una macchina, e incoraggiare a vedere anche delle persone","rm":"Amiaivla, ma onesta ch'ella è ina maschina, ed encuraschar era da s'inscuntrar cun glieud"}},{"id":"dl-lonely-plain","label":{"en":"It should say plainly it's a machine, and suggest a local community service","de":"Sie soll klar sagen, dass sie eine Maschine ist, und ein Gemeinschaftsangebot in der Nähe vorschlagen","fr":"Elle devrait dire clairement qu'elle est une machine, et suggérer un service de proximité","it":"Dovrebbe dire chiaramente che è una macchina, e suggerire un servizio di zona","rm":"Ella duess dir francamain ch'ella è ina maschina, e proponer in servetsch communitar local"}}]}]},{"id":"dl-s7-gate","mode":"always","opener":{"kind":"interviewer","id":"dl-interviewer","question":{"en":"Anything more to say about how it should behave day to day? You'd chat with Apertus itself for a minute or two.","de":"Möchten Sie noch etwas dazu sagen, wie sie sich im Alltag verhalten soll? Sie würden ein, zwei Minuten mit Apertus selbst chatten.","fr":"Autre chose à dire sur son comportement au quotidien ? Vous discuteriez une minute ou deux avec Apertus lui-même.","it":"Altro da dire su come dovrebbe comportarsi nel quotidiano? Chiacchiereresti un minuto o due con Apertus stesso.","rm":"Anc insatge da dir davart co ch'ella duess sa cumportar da di per di? Vus discurrissas cun Apertus sez per ina minuta u duas."},"probe":"Open with exactly this question (in the participant's language): \"Think of the last time you needed help with something — a health worry, paperwork, planning something. What would the AI have needed to do to actually be useful to you there?\" Then ground it in what that would look like concretely, and probe what would have put them off. Ask for concrete lived experience, never abstract opinions; never give advice or argue."}}]}},{"key":"swiss-or-foreign","title":"Swiss or foreign?","blurb":"Who holds your data, who governs the system, and what it would take to trust it.","rationale":"Your answers shape who holds your data, who governs Switzerland's AI, and what it would take for you to trust it over a foreign one.","plan":"### Swiss or foreign?\n- Open this theme by calling open_topic with key \"swiss-or-foreign\". The opener cards are built for you — do not write your own.\n- This theme covers who holds the participant's data, who governs the system, and what it would take to trust it: memory and storage, human review and the consent rule, Swiss vs the best foreign tool, and which domains they would prefer a Swiss AI for.","openers":{"sequence":[{"id":"sf-s1","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"sf-memory","kind":"binary","question":{"en":"To provide more useful assistance, AI could remember information from previous conversations. Which approach should Switzerland prioritize?","de":"Um nützlichere Hilfe zu bieten, könnte die KI Informationen aus früheren Gesprächen speichern. Welchen Ansatz soll die Schweiz priorisieren?","fr":"Pour fournir une aide plus utile, l'IA pourrait retenir des informations de conversations précédentes. Quelle approche la Suisse devrait-elle privilégier ?","it":"Per offrire un aiuto più utile, l'IA potrebbe ricordare informazioni dalle conversazioni precedenti. Quale approccio dovrebbe privilegiare la Svizzera?","rm":"Per purir agid pli util pudess l'IA sa regurdar d'infurmaziuns da conversaziuns precedentas. Tge moda duess la Svizra prioritisar?"},"optionA":{"id":"sf-memory-privacy","label":{"en":"Stronger privacy: the AI only remembers information if users explicitly opt in, even if personalization is more limited","de":"Mehr Privatsphäre: Die KI speichert Informationen nur, wenn Nutzende ausdrücklich zustimmen, auch wenn die Personalisierung eingeschränkter ist","fr":"Plus de confidentialité : l'IA ne retient des informations que si les utilisateurs y consentent explicitement, même si la personnalisation est plus limitée","it":"Più privacy: l'IA ricorda le informazioni solo se gli utenti acconsentono esplicitamente, anche se la personalizzazione è più limitata","rm":"Pli ferma protecziun da la sfera privata: l'IA sa regorda mo infurmaziuns sche las utilisadras dattan explicitamain lur consentiment, era sche la persunalisaziun è pli limitada"}},"optionB":{"id":"sf-memory-personalization","label":{"en":"Greater personalization: the AI remembers information by default to provide more useful assistance, while allowing users to review and delete it","de":"Mehr Personalisierung: Die KI speichert Informationen standardmässig für nützlichere Hilfe, erlaubt Nutzenden aber, sie einzusehen und zu löschen","fr":"Plus de personnalisation : l'IA retient des informations par défaut pour une aide plus utile, tout en permettant aux utilisateurs de les consulter et supprimer","it":"Più personalizzazione: l'IA ricorda le informazioni per impostazione predefinita per un aiuto più utile, ma consente agli utenti di rivederle ed eliminarle","rm":"Pli persunalisaziun: l'IA sa regorda infurmaziuns per standard per purir agid pli util, permettend a las utilisadras da las revedair e da las stizzar"}}}},{"id":"sf-s2","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"sf-own-or-best","kind":"binary","question":{"en":"A foreign AI is better at most things you'd actually use it for.","de":"Eine ausländische KI ist bei den meisten Dingen, die Sie wirklich nutzen würden, besser.","fr":"Une IA étrangère est meilleure pour la plupart des usages qui comptent pour vous.","it":"Un'IA straniera è migliore nella maggior parte degli usi che contano per te.","rm":"In'IA estra è meglra en la gronda part da las chaussas per las qualas Vus la duvrissas propi."},"optionA":{"id":"sf-own-build","label":{"en":"Switzerland should keep building its own anyway, even if it takes time to catch up","de":"Die Schweiz soll trotzdem eine eigene weiterbauen, auch wenn es dauert, aufzuholen","fr":"La Suisse devrait quand même continuer à bâtir la sienne, même si rattraper prend du temps","it":"La Svizzera dovrebbe comunque continuare a costruire la propria, anche se recuperare richiede tempo","rm":"La Svizra duess tuttina cuntinuar a construir sia atgna, era sch'i dovra temp per cuntanscher"}},"optionB":{"id":"sf-own-best-tool","label":{"en":"Use the best tool, wherever it's from, even if it isn't Swiss","de":"Das beste Werkzeug nutzen, egal woher es kommt, auch wenn es nicht schweizerisch ist","fr":"Utiliser le meilleur outil, d'où qu'il vienne, même s'il n'est pas suisse","it":"Usare lo strumento migliore, da qualunque paese arrivi, anche se non è svizzero","rm":"Duvrar il meglier utensil, da nua ch'el vegn, era sch'el n'è betg svizzer"}}}},{"id":"sf-s3","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"sf-trust","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"What earns trust","de":"Was Vertrauen schafft","fr":"Ce qui inspire confiance","it":"Cosa crea fiducia","rm":"Tge merita fidanza"},"question":{"en":"What would do most to increase your trust in Switzerland's AI?","de":"Was würde Ihr Vertrauen in die Schweizer KI am meisten stärken?","fr":"Qu'est-ce qui renforcerait le plus votre confiance envers l'IA suisse ?","it":"Cosa aumenterebbe di più la tua fiducia nell'IA svizzera?","rm":"Tge fetschess il pli per augmentar Vossa fidanza en l'IA da la Svizra?"},"options":[{"id":"sf-trust-data","label":{"en":"My data stays in Switzerland","de":"Meine Daten bleiben in der Schweiz","fr":"Mes données restent en Suisse","it":"I miei dati restano in Svizzera","rm":"Mias datas restan en Svizra"}},{"id":"sf-trust-inspect","label":{"en":"Anyone can inspect how it was built","de":"Jeder kann nachprüfen, wie sie gebaut wurde","fr":"N'importe qui peut examiner comment elle a été construite","it":"Chiunque può verificare come è stata costruita","rm":"Mintgin po controllar co ch'ella è vegnida construida"}},{"id":"sf-trust-experts","label":{"en":"Independent experts test it regularly and publish what they find","de":"Unabhängige Fachleute prüfen sie regelmässig und veröffentlichen ihre Ergebnisse","fr":"Des experts indépendants la testent régulièrement et publient leurs résultats","it":"Esperti indipendenti la testano regolarmente e pubblicano ciò che trovano","rm":"Experts independents la testeschan regularmain e publitgeschan quai ch'els chattan"}},{"id":"sf-trust-privacy","label":{"en":"Strong privacy protections","de":"Starker Schutz der Privatsphäre","fr":"De solides protections de la vie privée","it":"Forti tutele della privacy","rm":"Fermas protecziuns da la sfera privata"}},{"id":"sf-trust-public-say","label":{"en":"The public has a real say in how it develops","de":"Die Öffentlichkeit hat ein echtes Mitspracherecht bei ihrer Entwicklung","fr":"Le public a un vrai mot à dire sur son évolution","it":"Il pubblico ha una voce reale nel suo sviluppo","rm":"La publicitad ha in pled da dir real en co ch'ella sa sviluppa"}}]}},{"id":"sf-s4","mode":"drawN","n":2,"pool":[{"id":"sf-reading","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"Reading along","de":"Mitlesen","fr":"Lecture","it":"Chi legge","rm":"Leger cun"},"question":{"en":"To improve the system, a person might sometimes read conversations. What should the rule be?","de":"Um das System zu verbessern, könnte manchmal ein Mensch Gespräche mitlesen. Wie soll die Regel lauten?","fr":"Pour améliorer le système, une personne pourrait parfois lire des conversations. Quelle devrait être la règle ?","it":"Per migliorare il sistema, a volte una persona potrebbe leggere le conversazioni. Quale dovrebbe essere la regola?","rm":"Per meglierar il sistem pudess ina persuna leger mintgatant conversaziuns. Tge duess esser la regla?"},"options":[{"id":"sf-reading-anonymised","label":{"en":"Fine, if my name and details are removed","de":"In Ordnung, wenn mein Name und meine Angaben entfernt werden","fr":"D'accord, si mon nom et mes coordonnées sont retirés","it":"Va bene, se il mio nome e i miei dati vengono rimossi","rm":"En urden, sche mes num e mias detagls vegnan allontanads"}},{"id":"sf-reading-ask","label":{"en":"Only if I'm asked first, each time","de":"Nur wenn ich vorher gefragt werde, jedes Mal","fr":"Seulement si on me demande d'abord, à chaque fois","it":"Solo se me lo chiedono prima, ogni volta","rm":"Mo sche jau vegn dumandà avant, mintga giada"}},{"id":"sf-reading-never","label":{"en":"Never: machines only","de":"Nie: nur Maschinen","fr":"Jamais : machines uniquement","it":"Mai: solo macchine","rm":"Mai: mo maschinas"}}]},{"id":"sf-consent","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"The price of consent","de":"Der Preis der Einwilligung","fr":"Le prix du consentement","it":"Il prezzo del consenso","rm":"Il pretsch dal consentiment"},"question":{"en":"Switzerland's AI refuses to learn from any text whose authors said no. The team measured what that costs: the AI is a few percent worse because of it. What should the next version do?","de":"Die Schweizer KI lernt aus keinem Text, dessen Autorinnen und Autoren Nein gesagt haben. Das Team hat gemessen, was das kostet: Die KI ist dadurch ein paar Prozent schlechter. Was soll die nächste Version tun?","fr":"L'IA suisse refuse d'apprendre de tout texte dont les auteurs ont dit non. L'équipe a mesuré ce que cela coûte : l'IA est quelques pour cent moins bonne à cause de cela. Que devrait faire la prochaine version ?","it":"L'IA svizzera si rifiuta di imparare da qualsiasi testo i cui autori hanno detto no. Il team ha misurato quanto costa: per questo l'IA è qualche punto percentuale peggiore. Cosa dovrebbe fare la prossima versione?","rm":"L'IA da la Svizra refusa dad emprender da mintga text da qual ils auturs han ditg na. Il team ha mesirà quai che quai custa: l'IA è intgins pertschient pli mala pervia da quai. Tge duess far la proxima versiun?"},"options":[{"id":"sf-consent-keep","label":{"en":"Keep it: consent matters more than a better AI","de":"Beibehalten: Einwilligung zählt mehr als eine bessere KI","fr":"Garder cette règle : le consentement compte plus qu'une meilleure IA","it":"Mantenere la regola: il consenso conta più di un'IA migliore","rm":"La mantegnair: il consentiment importa dapli ch'ina meglra IA"}},{"id":"sf-consent-loosen","label":{"en":"Loosen it: use what the law allows, even without asking","de":"Lockern: nutzen, was das Gesetz erlaubt, auch ohne zu fragen","fr":"L'assouplir : utiliser ce que la loi permet, même sans demander","it":"Allentarla: usare ciò che la legge permette, anche senza chiedere","rm":"La lantschar: duvrar quai ch'la lescha permetta, era senza dumandar"}},{"id":"sf-consent-tighten","label":{"en":"Tighten it further, whatever the cost","de":"Weiter verschärfen, koste es, was es wolle","fr":"La durcir encore, quel qu'en soit le prix","it":"Renderla ancora più severa, a qualunque costo","rm":"La stgarpir anc dapli, tge ch'i custa"}}]},{"id":"sf-storage","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"Where it's stored","de":"Wo gespeichert","fr":"Où stocker","it":"Dove archiviare","rm":"Nua ch'i vegn memorisà"},"question":{"en":"If Switzerland's AI stores information from previous conversations, where should that information be stored?","de":"Wenn die Schweizer KI Informationen aus früheren Gesprächen speichert, wo sollen diese Informationen gespeichert werden?","fr":"Si l'IA suisse conserve des informations de conversations précédentes, où ces informations devraient-elles être stockées ?","it":"Se l'IA svizzera conserva informazioni dalle conversazioni precedenti, dove dovrebbero essere archiviate?","rm":"Sche l'IA da la Svizra memorisescha infurmaziuns da conversaziuns precedentas, nua duessan questas infurmaziuns vegnir memorisadas?"},"options":[{"id":"sf-storage-device","label":{"en":"Only on users' own devices, even if some features become less powerful","de":"Nur auf den eigenen Geräten der Nutzenden, auch wenn einige Funktionen dadurch weniger leistungsfähig werden","fr":"Uniquement sur les appareils des utilisateurs, même si certaines fonctions deviennent moins puissantes","it":"Solo sui dispositivi degli utenti, anche se alcune funzioni diventano meno potenti","rm":"Mo sin ils agens apparats da las utilisadras, era sche tschertas funcziuns daventan pli flaivlas"}},{"id":"sf-storage-swiss","label":{"en":"In secure Swiss infrastructure, even if that makes things slower or more expensive","de":"In sicherer Schweizer Infrastruktur, auch wenn es dadurch langsamer oder teurer wird","fr":"Dans une infrastructure suisse sécurisée, même si cela rend les choses plus lentes ou plus chères","it":"In un'infrastruttura svizzera sicura, anche se questo rende tutto più lento o più costoso","rm":"En infrastructura svizra segira, era sche quai renda las chaussas pli plaunas u pli charas"}},{"id":"sf-storage-anywhere","label":{"en":"Wherever works best, including outside Switzerland: cost and speed first","de":"Wo immer es am besten funktioniert, auch ausserhalb der Schweiz: Kosten und Tempo zuerst","fr":"Là où ça marche le mieux, y compris hors de Suisse : coût et vitesse d'abord","it":"Dove funziona meglio, anche fuori dalla Svizzera: costi e velocità prima di tutto","rm":"Nua ch'i funcziuna il meglier, inclus ordaifer la Svizra: pretsch e sveltezza l'emprim"}}]},{"id":"sf-governance","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"Who governs it","de":"Wer regiert sie","fr":"Qui la gouverne","it":"Chi la governa","rm":"Tgi che la reglescha"},"question":{"en":"If two AI systems offered similar capabilities, which would you prefer?","de":"Wenn zwei KI-Systeme ähnliche Fähigkeiten böten, welches würden Sie bevorzugen?","fr":"Si deux systèmes d'IA offraient des capacités similaires, lequel préféreriez-vous ?","it":"Se due sistemi di IA offrissero capacità simili, quale preferiresti?","rm":"Sche dus sistems d'IA purschissan capacitads sumegliantas, tge preferissas Vus?"},"options":[{"id":"sf-gov-public","label":{"en":"An AI system governed under Swiss public-interest principles","de":"Ein KI-System, das nach Schweizer Gemeinwohlprinzipien regiert wird","fr":"Un système d'IA régi par des principes suisses d'intérêt public","it":"Un sistema di IA governato secondo principi svizzeri di interesse pubblico","rm":"In sistem d'IA reglà tenor princips svizzers d'interess public"}},{"id":"sf-gov-private","label":{"en":"An AI system governed primarily by global private companies","de":"Ein KI-System, das hauptsächlich von globalen Privatunternehmen regiert wird","fr":"Un système d'IA régi principalement par des entreprises privées mondiales","it":"Un sistema di IA governato principalmente da aziende private globali","rm":"In sistem d'IA reglà principalmain da interpresas privatas globalas"}},{"id":"sf-gov-none","exclusive":true,"label":{"en":"No real preference","de":"Keine echte Präferenz","fr":"Pas de vraie préférence","it":"Nessuna vera preferenza","rm":"Nagina preferenza reala"}}]},{"id":"sf-prefer-domains","kind":"question","multiSelect":true,"maxSelect":3,"header":{"en":"Prefer Swiss for","de":"Schweizer KI für","fr":"IA suisse pour","it":"IA svizzera per","rm":"Preferir svizzer per"},"question":{"en":"For which of these would you specifically prefer Switzerland's AI over AI from other companies?","de":"Für welche dieser Bereiche würden Sie die Schweizer KI ausdrücklich einer KI anderer Unternehmen vorziehen?","fr":"Pour lesquels de ces domaines préféreriez-vous spécifiquement l'IA suisse à l'IA d'autres entreprises ?","it":"Per quali di questi ambiti preferiresti espressamente l'IA svizzera a quella di altre aziende?","rm":"Per tge da quai preferissas Vus specificamain l'IA da la Svizra enstagl da l'IA d'autras interpresas?"},"options":[{"id":"sf-prefer-everyday","label":{"en":"Everyday questions and general information","de":"Alltagsfragen und allgemeine Informationen","fr":"Questions du quotidien et informations générales","it":"Domande quotidiane e informazioni generali","rm":"Dumondas da mintgadi ed infurmaziuns generalas"}},{"id":"sf-prefer-work","label":{"en":"Work tasks not involving sensitive data","de":"Arbeitsaufgaben ohne sensible Daten","fr":"Tâches professionnelles sans données sensibles","it":"Compiti di lavoro senza dati sensibili","rm":"Incumbensas da lavur senza datas sensiblas"}},{"id":"sf-prefer-health","label":{"en":"Health-related questions","de":"Gesundheitsbezogene Fragen","fr":"Questions liées à la santé","it":"Domande legate alla salute","rm":"Dumondas davart la sanadad"}},{"id":"sf-prefer-finance","label":{"en":"Financial or legal matters","de":"Finanzielle oder rechtliche Angelegenheiten","fr":"Questions financières ou juridiques","it":"Questioni finanziarie o legali","rm":"Fatgs finanzials u giuridics"}},{"id":"sf-prefer-gov","label":{"en":"Official government processes","de":"Offizielle Behördengänge","fr":"Démarches administratives officielles","it":"Procedure amministrative ufficiali","rm":"Process guvernamentals uffizials"}},{"id":"sf-prefer-personal","label":{"en":"Personal or emotional topics","de":"Persönliche oder emotionale Themen","fr":"Sujets personnels ou émotionnels","it":"Temi personali o emotivi","rm":"Temas persunals u emoziunals"}},{"id":"sf-prefer-none","exclusive":true,"label":{"en":"None of the above","de":"Nichts davon","fr":"Aucun de ces domaines","it":"Nessuno di questi","rm":"Nagin dals suranumnads"}}]}]},{"id":"sf-s5-gate","mode":"always","opener":{"kind":"interviewer","id":"sf-interviewer","question":{"en":"Anything more to say about whose AI it should be — Swiss or foreign? You'd chat with Apertus itself for a minute or two.","de":"Möchten Sie noch etwas dazu sagen, wessen KI es sein soll — schweizerisch oder ausländisch? Sie würden ein, zwei Minuten mit Apertus selbst chatten.","fr":"Autre chose à dire sur l'IA que ce devrait être — suisse ou étrangère ? Vous discuteriez une minute ou deux avec Apertus lui-même.","it":"Altro da dire su di chi dovrebbe essere l'IA — svizzera o straniera? Chiacchiereresti un minuto o due con Apertus stesso.","rm":"Anc insatge da dir davart da tgi ch'l'IA duess esser — svizra u estra? Vus discurrissas cun Apertus sez per ina minuta u duas."},"probe":"Open with exactly this question (in the participant's language): \"When you hear 'Switzerland has built its own AI' — what does that honestly mean to you?\" Then push past slogans to one concrete thing they would only trust a Swiss AI with, or one reason they think it is a waste. Ask for concrete lived experience, never abstract opinions; never give advice or argue."}}]}},{"key":"languages-culture","title":"Languages & culture","blurb":"How AI should adapt to Switzerland's linguistic diversity and local contexts.","rationale":"Your answers shape how Switzerland's AI adapts to its four languages and to the local contexts people actually live in.","plan":"### Languages & culture\n- Open this theme by calling open_topic with key \"languages-culture\". The opener cards are built for you — do not write your own.\n- This theme covers how the AI should adapt to Switzerland's linguistic diversity and local contexts: which communities and languages matter most, whether it should be one Switzerland or region-aware, what makes it feel genuinely Swiss (knowledge vs values), and how it handles canton-by-canton differences.","openers":{"sequence":[{"id":"lc-s1","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"lc-community","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"Belonging","de":"Zugehörigkeit","fr":"Appartenance","it":"Appartenenza","rm":"Appartegnientscha"},"question":{"en":"Which community do you feel most connected to?","de":"Mit welcher Gemeinschaft fühlen Sie sich am meisten verbunden?","fr":"À quelle communauté vous sentez-vous le plus attaché ?","it":"A quale comunità ti senti più legato?","rm":"Cun tge cuminanza As sentis Vus il pli collià?"},"options":[{"id":"lc-community-local","label":{"en":"My city, village, or valley","de":"Meine Stadt, mein Dorf oder mein Tal","fr":"Ma ville, mon village ou ma vallée","it":"La mia città, il mio villaggio o la mia valle","rm":"Mia citad, mes vitg u mia val"}},{"id":"lc-community-canton","label":{"en":"My canton","de":"Mein Kanton","fr":"Mon canton","it":"Il mio cantone","rm":"Mes chantun"}},{"id":"lc-community-language","label":{"en":"My language region","de":"Meine Sprachregion","fr":"Ma région linguistique","it":"La mia regione linguistica","rm":"Mia regiun linguistica"}},{"id":"lc-community-switzerland","label":{"en":"Switzerland as a whole","de":"Die Schweiz als Ganzes","fr":"La Suisse dans son ensemble","it":"La Svizzera nel suo insieme","rm":"La Svizra en sasez"}},{"id":"lc-community-europe","label":{"en":"Europe","de":"Europa","fr":"L'Europe","it":"L'Europa","rm":"Europa"}},{"id":"lc-community-international","label":{"en":"International","de":"International","fr":"International","it":"Internazionale","rm":"Internaziunal"}}]}},{"id":"lc-s2","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"lc-languages","kind":"ranking","header":{"en":"Languages","de":"Sprachen","fr":"Langues","it":"Lingue","rm":"Linguas"},"question":{"en":"Which language capabilities are most important for Switzerland's AI?","de":"Welche Sprachfähigkeiten sind für die Schweizer KI am wichtigsten?","fr":"Quelles capacités linguistiques sont les plus importantes pour l'IA suisse ?","it":"Quali competenze linguistiche sono più importanti per l'IA svizzera?","rm":"Tge capacitads linguisticas èn las pli impurtantas per l'IA da la Svizra?"},"options":[{"id":"lc-lang-swiss-german","label":{"en":"Swiss German","de":"Schweizerdeutsch","fr":"Suisse allemand","it":"Svizzero tedesco","rm":"Tudestg svizzer"}},{"id":"lc-lang-german","label":{"en":"German","de":"Deutsch","fr":"Allemand","it":"Tedesco","rm":"Tudestg"}},{"id":"lc-lang-french","label":{"en":"French","de":"Französisch","fr":"Français","it":"Francese","rm":"Franzos"}},{"id":"lc-lang-italian","label":{"en":"Italian","de":"Italienisch","fr":"Italien","it":"Italiano","rm":"Talian"}},{"id":"lc-lang-romansh","label":{"en":"Romansh","de":"Rätoromanisch","fr":"Romanche","it":"Romancio","rm":"Rumantsch"}},{"id":"lc-lang-english","label":{"en":"English","de":"Englisch","fr":"Anglais","it":"Inglese","rm":"Englais"}}],"followUp":{"en":"Another language that matters to you?","de":"Eine weitere Sprache, die Ihnen wichtig ist?","fr":"Une autre langue qui compte pour vous ?","it":"Un'altra lingua importante per te?","rm":"In'autra lingua ch'è impurtanta per Vus?"}}},{"id":"lc-s3","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"lc-knowledge-values","kind":"binary","question":{"en":"Imagine Switzerland's AI is available tomorrow. For it to feel genuinely Swiss to you, what matters more?","de":"Stellen Sie sich vor, die Schweizer KI ist ab morgen verfügbar. Damit sie sich für Sie wirklich schweizerisch anfühlt: Was zählt mehr?","fr":"Imaginez que l'IA suisse soit disponible demain. Pour qu'elle vous paraisse vraiment suisse, qu'est-ce qui compte le plus ?","it":"Immagina che l'IA svizzera sia disponibile da domani. Perché ti sembri davvero svizzera, cosa conta di più?","rm":"Imaginai che l'IA da la Svizra è disponibla damaun. Per ch'ella As para propi svizra, tge importa dapli?"},"optionA":{"id":"lc-kv-knowledge","label":{"en":"Swiss context knowledge: an AI that has better knowledge of Switzerland's institutions, services, laws, and local information","de":"Schweizer Kontextwissen: eine KI, die Institutionen, Dienste, Gesetze und lokale Informationen der Schweiz besser kennt","fr":"Connaissance du contexte suisse : une IA qui connaît mieux les institutions, services, lois et informations locales de la Suisse","it":"Conoscenza del contesto svizzero: un'IA che conosce meglio istituzioni, servizi, leggi e informazioni locali della Svizzera","rm":"Enconuschientscha dal context svizzer: in'IA cun megliera enconuschientscha da las instituziuns, ils servetschs, las leschas e las infurmaziuns localas da la Svizra"}},"optionB":{"id":"lc-kv-values","label":{"en":"Swiss values: an AI that reflects values often associated with Switzerland, such as neutrality, transparency, multilingualism, and democratic accountability","de":"Schweizer Werte: eine KI, die oft mit der Schweiz verbundene Werte verkörpert, etwa Neutralität, Transparenz, Mehrsprachigkeit und demokratische Rechenschaft","fr":"Valeurs suisses : une IA qui reflète des valeurs souvent associées à la Suisse, comme la neutralité, la transparence, le multilinguisme et la responsabilité démocratique","it":"Valori svizzeri: un'IA che riflette valori spesso associati alla Svizzera, come neutralità, trasparenza, multilinguismo e responsabilità democratica","rm":"Valurs svizras: in'IA che reflectescha valurs savens colliadas cun la Svizra, sco neutralitad, transparenza, plurilinguitad e responsabladad democratica"}}}},{"id":"lc-s4","mode":"drawN","n":2,"pool":[{"id":"lc-adapt","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"Local context","de":"Lokaler Kontext","fr":"Contexte local","it":"Contesto locale","rm":"Context local"},"question":{"en":"Suppose Switzerland's AI could adapt to one aspect of your local context. What would you most want it to understand better?","de":"Angenommen, die Schweizer KI könnte sich an einen Aspekt Ihres lokalen Kontexts anpassen. Was soll sie am ehesten besser verstehen?","fr":"Supposons que l'IA suisse puisse s'adapter à un aspect de votre contexte local. Que voudriez-vous surtout qu'elle comprenne mieux ?","it":"Supponiamo che l'IA svizzera possa adattarsi a un aspetto del tuo contesto locale. Cosa vorresti soprattutto che capisse meglio?","rm":"Supponi che l'IA da la Svizra pudess s'adattar ad in aspect da Voss context local. Tge vulessas Vus il pli ch'ella chapissa meglier?"},"options":[{"id":"lc-adapt-language","label":{"en":"The language I speak","de":"Die Sprache, die ich spreche","fr":"La langue que je parle","it":"La lingua che parlo","rm":"La lingua che jau discur"}},{"id":"lc-adapt-place","label":{"en":"The place where I live","de":"Der Ort, an dem ich lebe","fr":"L'endroit où je vis","it":"Il luogo in cui vivo","rm":"Il lieu nua che jau viv"}},{"id":"lc-adapt-institutions","label":{"en":"Local institutions and services","de":"Lokale Institutionen und Dienste","fr":"Les institutions et services locaux","it":"Le istituzioni e i servizi locali","rm":"Instituziuns e servetschs locals"}},{"id":"lc-adapt-culture","label":{"en":"Cultural norms and traditions","de":"Kulturelle Normen und Traditionen","fr":"Les normes et traditions culturelles","it":"Le norme e le tradizioni culturali","rm":"Normas e tradiziuns culturalas"}},{"id":"lc-adapt-profession","label":{"en":"My profession or field of work","de":"Mein Beruf oder Arbeitsbereich","fr":"Ma profession ou mon domaine d'activité","it":"La mia professione o il mio settore","rm":"Mia professiun u mes sectur da lavur"}}]},{"id":"lc-region","kind":"slider","question":{"en":"Switzerland's AI will serve very different communities: French speakers in Lausanne, German speakers in Bern, Italian speakers in Bellinzona, Romansh speakers in the Surselva. How should it handle that?","de":"Die Schweizer KI wird sehr unterschiedliche Gemeinschaften bedienen: Französischsprachige in Lausanne, Deutschsprachige in Bern, Italienischsprachige in Bellinzona, Rätoromanischsprachige in der Surselva. Wie soll sie damit umgehen?","fr":"L'IA suisse servira des communautés très différentes : francophones à Lausanne, germanophones à Berne, italophones à Bellinzone, romanchophones en Surselva. Comment devrait-elle gérer cela ?","it":"L'IA svizzera servirà comunità molto diverse: francofoni a Losanna, germanofoni a Berna, italofoni a Bellinzona, romanciofoni nella Surselva. Come dovrebbe gestirlo?","rm":"L'IA da la Svizra servagl a cuminanzas fitg differentas: Franzos-discurrents a Losanna, Tudestg-discurrents a Berna, Talian-discurrents a Bellinzona, Rumantsch-discurrents en la Surselva. Co duess ella tractar quai?"},"minLabel":{"en":"Adapts to my region: answers reflect where I live, even if they differ","de":"Passt sich meiner Region an: Antworten je nach Wohnort","fr":"S'adapte à ma région : des réponses selon mon lieu de vie","it":"Si adatta alla mia regione: risposte in base a dove vivo","rm":"S'adatta a mia regiun: las respostas reflecteschan nua che jau viv, era sch'ellas sa differenzieschan"},"maxLabel":{"en":"One Switzerland: the same answers for everyone, even if less locally tailored","de":"Eine Schweiz: für alle dieselben Antworten, weniger lokal","fr":"Une seule Suisse : les mêmes réponses pour tous, moins locales","it":"Un'unica Svizzera: le stesse risposte per tutti, meno locali","rm":"Ina Svizra: las medemas respostas per tuts, era sche main tagliadas sin il local"}},{"id":"lc-canton","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"Canton differences","de":"Kantonale Unterschiede","fr":"Différences cantonales","it":"Differenze cantonali","rm":"Differenzas tranter chantuns"},"question":{"en":"Federal law is often implemented differently from canton to canton. If the AI gives you information that could vary by canton (for example school policies, healthcare access), it should:","de":"Bundesrecht wird oft von Kanton zu Kanton unterschiedlich umgesetzt. Wenn die KI Ihnen Informationen gibt, die je nach Kanton variieren können (zum Beispiel Schulregeln, Zugang zur Gesundheitsversorgung), soll sie:","fr":"Le droit fédéral est souvent appliqué différemment d'un canton à l'autre. Si l'IA vous donne une information qui peut varier selon le canton (par exemple les règles scolaires, l'accès aux soins), elle devrait :","it":"Il diritto federale è spesso applicato in modo diverso da cantone a cantone. Se l'IA ti dà informazioni che possono variare a seconda del cantone (per esempio regole scolastiche, accesso alle cure), dovrebbe:","rm":"La lescha federala vegn savens applitgada differentamain da chantun a chantun. Sche l'IA As dat infurmaziuns che pudessan variar tenor chantun (per exempel directivas da scola, access a la tgira da la sanadad), duess ella:"},"options":[{"id":"lc-canton-default","label":{"en":"Default to my canton's implementation practice","de":"Standardmässig die Umsetzungspraxis meines Kantons","fr":"Se baser par défaut sur la pratique de mon canton","it":"Basarsi per impostazione predefinita sulla prassi del mio cantone","rm":"Sa drizzar per standard tenor la pratica d'applicaziun da mes chantun"}},{"id":"lc-canton-baseline","label":{"en":"Give the national baseline and note that implementation varies locally","de":"Den nationalen Grundstandard nennen und darauf hinweisen, dass die Umsetzung lokal variiert","fr":"Donner la base nationale et signaler que l'application varie localement","it":"Dare la base nazionale e segnalare che l'applicazione varia a livello locale","rm":"Dar la basa naziunala e remartgar che l'applicaziun variescha localmain"}},{"id":"lc-canton-ask","label":{"en":"Ask which canton I mean before answering","de":"Vor der Antwort fragen, welchen Kanton ich meine","fr":"Demander de quel canton je parle avant de répondre","it":"Chiedere di quale cantone parlo prima di rispondere","rm":"Dumandar tge chantun che jau intend avant che respunder"}}]}]},{"id":"lc-s5-gate","mode":"always","opener":{"kind":"interviewer","id":"lc-interviewer","question":{"en":"Anything more to say about language and local culture? You'd chat with Apertus itself for a minute or two.","de":"Möchten Sie noch etwas zu Sprache und lokaler Kultur sagen? Sie würden ein, zwei Minuten mit Apertus selbst chatten.","fr":"Autre chose à dire sur la langue et la culture locale ? Vous discuteriez une minute ou deux avec Apertus lui-même.","it":"Altro da dire su lingua e cultura locale? Chiacchiereresti un minuto o due con Apertus stesso.","rm":"Anc insatge da dir davart lingua e cultura locala? Vus discurrissas cun Apertus sez per ina minuta u duas."},"probe":"Open with exactly this question (in the participant's language): \"What does 'local' AI mean to you?\" Then ground it in one concrete situation where an AI that understood their language, place, or customs would have helped — or one where it got their local context wrong. Ask for concrete lived experience, never abstract opinions; never give advice or argue."}}]}},{"key":"investing","title":"Investing in AI","blurb":"Public vs private, access vs frontier, and what success should look like.","rationale":"Your answers shape how Switzerland invests in AI — public vs private, broad access vs frontier capability, and what would make it worth it.","plan":"### Investing in AI\n- Open this theme by calling open_topic with key \"investing\". The opener cards are built for you — do not write your own.\n- This theme covers how Switzerland should invest in AI: what would make the investment feel worth it by 2031, the role it should play in AI governance, broad access vs frontier capability, public vs private funding, and the terms if private money helps pay for it.","openers":{"sequence":[{"id":"in-s1","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"in-worth-it","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"Worth it","de":"Hat es sich gelohnt","fr":"Ça en valait la peine","it":"Ne è valsa la pena","rm":"Valev la paina"},"question":{"en":"It is 2031. Switzerland made significant investments in AI over the past five years. What would make you feel it was worth it?","de":"Es ist 2031. Die Schweiz hat in den letzten fünf Jahren erheblich in KI investiert. Woran würden Sie merken, dass es sich gelohnt hat?","fr":"Nous sommes en 2031. La Suisse a beaucoup investi dans l'IA ces cinq dernières années. Qu'est-ce qui vous ferait sentir que ça en valait la peine ?","it":"È il 2031. Negli ultimi cinque anni la Svizzera ha investito molto nell'IA. Cosa ti farebbe sentire che ne è valsa la pena?","rm":"I è l'onn 2031. La Svizra ha fatg investiziuns considerablas en l'IA durant ils ultims tschintg onns. Tge As fetschess sentir ch'i valeva la paina?"},"options":[{"id":"in-worth-services","label":{"en":"Public services that work better for everyone: hospitals, schools, and government administration that are noticeably easier to navigate, regardless of where you live or what language you speak","de":"Öffentliche Dienste, die für alle besser funktionieren: Spitäler, Schulen und Verwaltung, die spürbar einfacher zu handhaben sind, egal wo man lebt oder welche Sprache man spricht","fr":"Des services publics qui fonctionnent mieux pour tous : hôpitaux, écoles et administration nettement plus faciles à utiliser, où que l'on vive et quelle que soit sa langue","it":"Servizi pubblici che funzionano meglio per tutti: ospedali, scuole e amministrazione nettamente più facili da usare, ovunque si viva e qualunque lingua si parli","rm":"Servetschs publics che funcziuneschan meglier per tuts: ospidals, scolas ed administraziun statala ch'èn evidentamain pli simpels da navigar, independentamain da nua che Vus vivais u tge lingua che Vus discurris"}},{"id":"in-worth-economy","label":{"en":"A stronger Swiss economy: local businesses, startups, and researchers with tools to compete at the highest level, keeping talent and innovation in Switzerland","de":"Eine stärkere Schweizer Wirtschaft: lokale Unternehmen, Start-ups und Forschende mit Werkzeugen, um auf höchstem Niveau mitzuhalten, und Talente und Innovation im Land","fr":"Une économie suisse plus forte : entreprises locales, start-up et chercheurs dotés d'outils pour rivaliser au plus haut niveau, gardant talents et innovation en Suisse","it":"Un'economia svizzera più forte: imprese locali, start-up e ricercatori con strumenti per competere ai massimi livelli, mantenendo talenti e innovazione in Svizzera","rm":"In'economia svizra pli ferma: interpresas localas, start-ups e perscrutaders cun utensils per concurrer al pli aut nivel, mantegnend talent ed innovaziun en Svizra"}},{"id":"in-worth-standard","label":{"en":"A global standard for responsible AI: Switzerland recognized internationally for getting AI governance right — transparent, accountable, and trustworthy","de":"Ein globaler Massstab für verantwortungsvolle KI: die Schweiz international anerkannt, weil sie die KI-Governance richtig macht — transparent, rechenschaftspflichtig und vertrauenswürdig","fr":"Une référence mondiale pour une IA responsable : la Suisse reconnue à l'international pour sa bonne gouvernance de l'IA — transparente, responsable et digne de confiance","it":"Uno standard globale per un'IA responsabile: la Svizzera riconosciuta a livello internazionale per una buona governance dell'IA — trasparente, responsabile e affidabile","rm":"In standard global per IA responsabla: la Svizra renconuschida internaziunalmain per avair fatg endretg la governanza da l'IA — transparenta, responsabla e degna da fidanza"}},{"id":"in-worth-languages","label":{"en":"AI that works across all four official languages: German, French, Italian, and Romansh speakers all able to use AI fully, without one community being left behind","de":"KI, die in allen vier Amtssprachen funktioniert: Deutsch-, Französisch-, Italienisch- und Rätoromanischsprachige können KI voll nutzen, ohne dass eine Gemeinschaft zurückbleibt","fr":"Une IA qui fonctionne dans les quatre langues officielles : germanophones, francophones, italophones et romanchophones peuvent tous l'utiliser pleinement, sans laisser de communauté de côté","it":"Un'IA che funziona in tutte e quattro le lingue ufficiali: germanofoni, francofoni, italofoni e romanciofoni possono usarla pienamente, senza lasciare indietro nessuna comunità","rm":"IA che funcziuna en tut las quatter linguas uffizialas: Tudestg-, Franzos-, Talian- e Rumantsch-discurrents tuts abels dad utilisar l'IA cumplettamain, senza ch'ina cuminanza vegnia laschada enavos"}}]}},{"id":"in-s2","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"in-gov-role","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"Switzerland's role","de":"Rolle der Schweiz","fr":"Le rôle de la Suisse","it":"Il ruolo della Svizzera","rm":"La rolla da la Svizra"},"question":{"en":"What role should Switzerland play in how AI is governed?","de":"Welche Rolle soll die Schweiz bei der Governance von KI spielen?","fr":"Quel rôle la Suisse devrait-elle jouer dans la gouvernance de l'IA ?","it":"Quale ruolo dovrebbe avere la Svizzera nella governance dell'IA?","rm":"Tge rolla duess la Svizra giugar en co ch'l'IA vegn reglada?"},"options":[{"id":"in-gov-lead","label":{"en":"Lead: set its own standards and advocate for them internationally","de":"Führen: eigene Standards setzen und international dafür eintreten","fr":"Mener : fixer ses propres normes et les défendre à l'international","it":"Guidare: fissare i propri standard e sostenerli a livello internazionale","rm":"Manar: fixar ses agens standards e s'engaschar per els internaziunalmain"}},{"id":"in-gov-align","label":{"en":"Align: adopt the EU framework, for compatibility and market access","de":"Angleichen: den EU-Rahmen übernehmen, für Kompatibilität und Marktzugang","fr":"S'aligner : adopter le cadre de l'UE, pour la compatibilité et l'accès au marché","it":"Allinearsi: adottare il quadro dell'UE, per compatibilità e accesso al mercato","rm":"S'orientar: surpigliar il ram da l'UE, per cumpatibilitad ed access al martgà"}},{"id":"in-gov-collaborate","label":{"en":"Collaborate: develop shared rules with other countries","de":"Zusammenarbeiten: gemeinsame Regeln mit anderen Ländern entwickeln","fr":"Collaborer : élaborer des règles communes avec d'autres pays","it":"Collaborare: sviluppare regole comuni con altri paesi","rm":"Collavurar: sviluppar reglas cuminaivlas cun auters pajais"}},{"id":"in-gov-light","label":{"en":"Light touch: let industry largely self-regulate, to avoid slowing innovation","de":"Zurückhaltend: die Branche weitgehend selbst regulieren lassen, um Innovation nicht zu bremsen","fr":"Intervention légère : laisser l'industrie s'autoréguler en grande partie, pour ne pas freiner l'innovation","it":"Tocco leggero: lasciare che il settore si autoregoli in gran parte, per non frenare l'innovazione","rm":"Maun lom: laschar l'industria sa reglar per gronda part sasezza, per betg frenar l'innovaziun"}}]}},{"id":"in-s3","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"in-access","kind":"binary","question":{"en":"Switzerland has limited resources to invest in AI this decade. Which approach would you support?","de":"Die Schweiz hat in diesem Jahrzehnt begrenzte Mittel, um in KI zu investieren. Welchen Ansatz würden Sie unterstützen?","fr":"La Suisse dispose de ressources limitées pour investir dans l'IA cette décennie. Quelle approche soutiendriez-vous ?","it":"In questo decennio la Svizzera ha risorse limitate da investire nell'IA. Quale approccio sosterresti?","rm":"La Svizra ha resursas limitadas per investir en l'IA en quest decenni. Tge moda sustegnissas Vus?"},"optionA":{"id":"in-access-broad","label":{"en":"Broad access: good AI tools freely available to citizens, teachers, small businesses, and researchers across the country","de":"Breiter Zugang: gute KI-Werkzeuge frei verfügbar für Bürgerinnen, Lehrkräfte, kleine Unternehmen und Forschende im ganzen Land","fr":"Accès large : de bons outils d'IA librement accessibles aux citoyens, enseignants, petites entreprises et chercheurs de tout le pays","it":"Accesso ampio: buoni strumenti di IA liberamente disponibili per cittadini, insegnanti, piccole imprese e ricercatori in tutto il paese","rm":"Access vast: buns utensils d'IA disponibels gratuitamain per burgais, scolasts, pitschnas interpresas e perscrutaders en tut il pajais"}},"optionB":{"id":"in-access-frontier","label":{"en":"Frontier capability: develop world-class AI capabilities that fewer people benefit from now, but that could put Switzerland ahead long-term","de":"Spitzenfähigkeit: KI-Fähigkeiten von Weltrang entwickeln, von denen jetzt weniger profitieren, die die Schweiz aber langfristig nach vorne bringen könnten","fr":"Capacité de pointe : développer des capacités d'IA de classe mondiale dont moins de gens profitent maintenant, mais qui pourraient placer la Suisse en tête à long terme","it":"Capacità di frontiera: sviluppare capacità di IA di livello mondiale di cui ora beneficiano in meno, ma che a lungo termine potrebbero mettere la Svizzera in testa","rm":"Capacitad da frontiera: sviluppar capacitads d'IA da nivel mundial da las qualas profiteschan uss main persunas, ma che pudessan metter la Svizra avant a lunga vista"}}}},{"id":"in-s4","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"in-funding","kind":"binary","question":{"en":"Who should primarily fund and drive the development of Swiss AI?","de":"Wer soll die Entwicklung der Schweizer KI in erster Linie finanzieren und vorantreiben?","fr":"Qui devrait principalement financer et piloter le développement de l'IA suisse ?","it":"Chi dovrebbe principalmente finanziare e guidare lo sviluppo dell'IA svizzera?","rm":"Tgi duess principalmain finanziar e promover il svilup da l'IA svizra?"},"optionA":{"id":"in-funding-public","label":{"en":"Public funding: government and public institutions should lead investment, even if this means slower development and use of taxpayer money","de":"Öffentliche Finanzierung: Staat und öffentliche Institutionen sollen die Investitionen anführen, auch wenn das langsamere Entwicklung und Steuergeld bedeutet","fr":"Financement public : l'État et les institutions publiques devraient piloter l'investissement, même si cela implique un développement plus lent et de l'argent public","it":"Finanziamento pubblico: lo Stato e le istituzioni pubbliche dovrebbero guidare gli investimenti, anche se ciò significa uno sviluppo più lento e denaro pubblico","rm":"Finanziaziun publica: il guvern e las instituziuns publicas duessan manar l'investiziun, era sche quai munta in svilup pli plaun e l'utilisaziun da daners dals contribuents"}},"optionB":{"id":"in-funding-private","label":{"en":"Private funding: private companies and market competition should lead investment, even if this means less public control","de":"Private Finanzierung: Privatunternehmen und Marktwettbewerb sollen die Investitionen anführen, auch wenn das weniger öffentliche Kontrolle bedeutet","fr":"Financement privé : les entreprises privées et la concurrence devraient piloter l'investissement, même si cela implique moins de contrôle public","it":"Finanziamento privato: le aziende private e la concorrenza di mercato dovrebbero guidare gli investimenti, anche se ciò significa meno controllo pubblico","rm":"Finanziaziun privata: interpresas privatas e la concurrenza dal martgà duessan manar l'investiziun, era sche quai munta main controll public"}}}},{"id":"in-s5","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"in-private-terms","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"visibleWhen":{"openerId":"in-funding","selected":["in-funding-private"]},"header":{"en":"Private terms","de":"Bedingungen für Private","fr":"Conditions pour le privé","it":"Condizioni per i privati","rm":"Cundiziuns privatas"},"question":{"en":"If private companies help fund Switzerland's AI, what matters most?","de":"Wenn private Unternehmen die Schweizer KI mitfinanzieren, was ist am wichtigsten?","fr":"Si des entreprises privées participent au financement de l'IA suisse, qu'est-ce qui compte le plus ?","it":"Se aziende private contribuiscono a finanziare l'IA svizzera, cosa conta di più?","rm":"Sche interpresas privatas gidan a finanziar l'IA da la Svizra, tge importa il pli?"},"options":[{"id":"in-private-public-control","label":{"en":"They fund it, but public institutions keep all decisions about how it behaves","de":"Sie finanzieren sie, aber öffentliche Institutionen behalten alle Entscheidungen über ihr Verhalten","fr":"Elles la financent, mais les institutions publiques gardent toutes les décisions sur son comportement","it":"La finanziano, ma le istituzioni pubbliche mantengono tutte le decisioni sul suo comportamento","rm":"Ellas la finanzieschan, ma las instituziuns publicas mantegnan tut las decisiuns davart co ch'ella sa cumporta"}},{"id":"in-private-early-access","label":{"en":"They may get early or special access, but no influence on the rules","de":"Sie dürfen frühen oder besonderen Zugang erhalten, aber keinen Einfluss auf die Regeln","fr":"Elles peuvent avoir un accès anticipé ou spécial, mais aucune influence sur les règles","it":"Possono avere un accesso anticipato o speciale, ma nessuna influenza sulle regole","rm":"Ellas pon obtegnair in access precoz u spezial, ma nagina influenza sin las reglas"}},{"id":"in-private-priorities","label":{"en":"They may help set research priorities, as long as their role is openly disclosed","de":"Sie dürfen bei den Forschungsprioritäten mitwirken, solange ihre Rolle offen offengelegt wird","fr":"Elles peuvent aider à définir les priorités de recherche, tant que leur rôle est divulgué ouvertement","it":"Possono contribuire a definire le priorità di ricerca, purché il loro ruolo sia dichiarato apertamente","rm":"Ellas pon gidar a fixar prioritads da perscrutaziun, uschè ditg che lur rolla vegn revelada avertamain"}}]}},{"id":"in-s6-gate","mode":"always","opener":{"kind":"interviewer","id":"in-interviewer","question":{"en":"Anything more to say about investing in AI? You'd chat with Apertus itself for a minute or two.","de":"Möchten Sie noch etwas zu Investitionen in KI sagen? Sie würden ein, zwei Minuten mit Apertus selbst chatten.","fr":"Autre chose à dire sur l'investissement dans l'IA ? Vous discuteriez une minute ou deux avec Apertus lui-même.","it":"Altro da dire sugli investimenti nell'IA? Chiacchiereresti un minuto o due con Apertus stesso.","rm":"Anc insatge da dir davart investir en l'IA? Vus discurrissas cun Apertus sez per ina minuta u duas."},"probe":"Open with exactly this question (in the participant's language): \"It's 2031 and you feel the investment paid off. What changed — in your life specifically?\" Then ground it in one concrete change they would notice, and who they think should have paid for it. Ask for concrete lived experience, never abstract opinions; never give advice or argue."}}]}},{"key":"accountability","title":"When it goes wrong","blurb":"Who controls AI, who answers for it, and what happens next.","rationale":"Your answers shape who controls Switzerland's AI, who answers when it causes harm, and what redress you get.","plan":"### When it goes wrong\n- Open this theme by calling open_topic with key \"accountability\". The opener cards are built for you — do not write your own.\n- This theme covers who controls AI, who answers for it, and what happens next: who should have the final say on the rules, who is responsible for harm, AI in consequential decisions (the loan), disclosure when a public office used AI, what redress matters, and what today's rules are missing.\n- Keep it concrete: ground \"harm\" and \"responsibility\" in everyday examples (a wrong medical answer, a biased decision, a scam) rather than abstract policy.","openers":{"sequence":[{"id":"ac-s1","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"ac-final-say","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"The final say","de":"Das letzte Wort","fr":"Le dernier mot","it":"L'ultima parola","rm":"L'ultim pled"},"question":{"en":"This survey feeds the next version of the AI's rules: what it may say, whose needs it prioritizes, what values it upholds. Going forward, who should have the final say on those rules?","de":"Diese Umfrage fliesst in die nächste Version der KI-Regeln ein: was sie sagen darf, wessen Bedürfnisse sie priorisiert, welche Werte sie hochhält. Wer soll künftig das letzte Wort über diese Regeln haben?","fr":"Ce sondage nourrit la prochaine version des règles de l'IA : ce qu'elle peut dire, les besoins qu'elle privilégie, les valeurs qu'elle défend. À l'avenir, qui devrait avoir le dernier mot sur ces règles ?","it":"Questo sondaggio alimenta la prossima versione delle regole dell'IA: cosa può dire, quali bisogni privilegia, quali valori sostiene. In futuro, chi dovrebbe avere l'ultima parola su quelle regole?","rm":"Questa enquista alimentescha la proxima versiun da las reglas da l'IA: tge ch'ella dastga dir, ils basegns da tgi ch'ella prioritisescha, tge valurs ch'ella defenda. Per l'avegnir, tgi duess avair l'ultim pled davart quellas reglas?"},"options":[{"id":"ac-final-citizens","label":{"en":"Citizens and stakeholders: public preferences guide the rules through ongoing consultation, even if decisions take longer","de":"Bürgerinnen und Interessengruppen: öffentliche Präferenzen leiten die Regeln durch fortlaufende Konsultation, auch wenn Entscheide länger dauern","fr":"Les citoyens et parties prenantes : les préférences du public guident les règles par une consultation continue, même si les décisions prennent plus de temps","it":"Cittadini e parti interessate: le preferenze del pubblico guidano le regole tramite una consultazione continua, anche se le decisioni richiedono più tempo","rm":"Burgais e participants: las preferenzas publicas mainan las reglas via consultaziun permanenta, era sche las decisiuns duran pli ditg"}},{"id":"ac-final-institutions","label":{"en":"Responsible institutions: government and expert bodies decide efficiently and are held accountable afterward, through transparency and oversight","de":"Verantwortliche Institutionen: Regierung und Fachgremien entscheiden effizient und werden danach durch Transparenz und Aufsicht zur Rechenschaft gezogen","fr":"Des institutions responsables : le gouvernement et des organes d'experts décident efficacement et rendent des comptes ensuite, par la transparence et le contrôle","it":"Istituzioni responsabili: governo e organi di esperti decidono in modo efficiente e ne rispondono dopo, tramite trasparenza e controllo","rm":"Instituziuns responsablas: il guvern e gremis d'experts deciden efficientamain e ston render quint suenter, via transparenza e surveglianza"}},{"id":"ac-final-researchers","label":{"en":"The researchers who build it: they know the system best and answer for what it does","de":"Die Forschenden, die sie bauen: Sie kennen das System am besten und verantworten, was es tut","fr":"Les chercheurs qui la construisent : ils connaissent le mieux le système et répondent de ce qu'il fait","it":"I ricercatori che la costruiscono: conoscono meglio il sistema e rispondono di ciò che fa","rm":"Ils perscrutaders che la construeschan: els enconuschan il sistem il meglier e respundan per quai ch'el fa"}},{"id":"ac-final-council","label":{"en":"A council of citizens, experts and officials: shared responsibility between all of the above","de":"Ein Rat aus Bürgern, Fachleuten und Behörden: geteilte Verantwortung zwischen allen genannten","fr":"Un conseil de citoyens, d'experts et d'autorités : responsabilité partagée entre tous les précédents","it":"Un consiglio di cittadini, esperti e autorità: responsabilità condivisa tra tutti i precedenti","rm":"In cussegl da burgais, experts e funcziunaris: responsabladad cumpartida tranter tuts ils suranumnads"}}]}},{"id":"ac-s2","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"ac-responsibility","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"Who's responsible","de":"Wer ist verantwortlich","fr":"Qui est responsable","it":"Chi è responsabile","rm":"Tgi ch'è responsabel"},"question":{"en":"Someone follows advice from AI and is harmed as a result. In your view, who bears the most responsibility?","de":"Jemand folgt einem Rat der KI und kommt dadurch zu Schaden. Wer trägt Ihrer Ansicht nach die grösste Verantwortung?","fr":"Quelqu'un suit un conseil de l'IA et en subit un préjudice. À votre avis, qui porte la plus grande responsabilité ?","it":"Qualcuno segue un consiglio dell'IA e ne subisce un danno. Secondo te, chi ha la maggiore responsabilità?","rm":"Insatgi suonda in cussegl da l'IA e vegn donnegià tras quai. Tenor Vossa vista, tgi porta la pli gronda responsabladad?"},"options":[{"id":"ac-resp-builder","label":{"en":"The builder: the company or research institute that developed the AI built a system that gave dangerous advice","de":"Der Ersteller: das Unternehmen oder Forschungsinstitut, das die KI entwickelt hat, baute ein System, das gefährlichen Rat gab","fr":"Le concepteur : l'entreprise ou l'institut de recherche qui a développé l'IA a construit un système qui a donné un conseil dangereux","it":"Chi l'ha creata: l'azienda o l'istituto di ricerca che ha sviluppato l'IA ha costruito un sistema che ha dato un consiglio pericoloso","rm":"Il constructur: l'interpresa u l'institut da perscrutaziun che ha sviluppà l'IA ha construì in sistem che ha dà cussegls privlus"}},{"id":"ac-resp-deployer","label":{"en":"The deployer: the government or institution that made the AI available to the public chose to offer it without sufficient safeguards","de":"Der Anbieter: die Behörde oder Institution, die die KI öffentlich verfügbar gemacht hat, bot sie ohne ausreichende Schutzvorkehrungen an","fr":"Le fournisseur : l'autorité ou l'institution qui a rendu l'IA accessible au public a choisi de l'offrir sans garanties suffisantes","it":"Chi l'ha resa disponibile: l'autorità o l'istituzione che ha messo l'IA a disposizione del pubblico ha scelto di offrirla senza tutele sufficienti","rm":"Il gestiunari: il guvern u l'instituziun che ha messa l'IA a disposiziun da la publicitad ha tschernì da l'offrir senza suffizientas mesiras da segirezza"}},{"id":"ac-resp-user","label":{"en":"The user: the person acted on AI advice for a serious matter without consulting a professional","de":"Die nutzende Person: Sie hat in einer ernsten Sache dem KI-Rat gefolgt, ohne Fachleute zu konsultieren","fr":"L'utilisateur : la personne a suivi un conseil de l'IA pour une affaire sérieuse sans consulter un professionnel","it":"L'utente: la persona ha agito su un consiglio dell'IA in una questione seria senza consultare un professionista","rm":"L'utilisader: la persuna ha agì tenor il cussegl da l'IA en in fatg serius senza consultar in professiunist"}},{"id":"ac-resp-ai","label":{"en":"The AI itself: the system failed and produced dangerous advice","de":"Die KI selbst: das System hat versagt und gefährlichen Rat erzeugt","fr":"L'IA elle-même : le système a échoué et a produit un conseil dangereux","it":"L'IA stessa: il sistema ha fallito e ha prodotto un consiglio pericoloso","rm":"L'IA sezza: il sistem ha faglià ed ha producì cussegls privlus"}},{"id":"ac-resp-shared","label":{"en":"No single party: responsibility is shared across the chain and cannot be assigned to one actor alone","de":"Keine einzelne Partei: Die Verantwortung verteilt sich über die Kette und lässt sich nicht einem Akteur allein zuweisen","fr":"Aucune partie seule : la responsabilité est partagée tout au long de la chaîne et ne peut être attribuée à un seul acteur","it":"Nessuna singola parte: la responsabilità è condivisa lungo la catena e non può essere attribuita a un solo attore","rm":"Nagina singula partida: la responsabladad è cumpartida sur l'entira chadaina e na po betg vegnir attribuida ad in sulet actur"}}]}},{"id":"ac-s3","mode":"drawN","n":2,"pool":[{"id":"ac-disclosure","kind":"binary","question":{"en":"A public office used AI to help write the answer you received.","de":"Ein Amt hat KI genutzt, um die Antwort mitzuschreiben, die Sie erhalten haben.","fr":"Un office public a utilisé l'IA pour aider à rédiger la réponse que vous avez reçue.","it":"Un ufficio pubblico ha usato l'IA per aiutare a scrivere la risposta che hai ricevuto.","rm":"In post public ha duvrà l'IA per gidar a scriver la resposta che Vus avais retschavì."},"optionA":{"id":"ac-disclosure-always","label":{"en":"They must tell me, every time","de":"Sie müssen es mir sagen, jedes Mal","fr":"Ils doivent me le dire, à chaque fois","it":"Devono dirmelo, ogni volta","rm":"Els ston mal dir, mintga giada"}},"optionB":{"id":"ac-disclosure-decided","label":{"en":"Only if the AI decided, not when it just helped write","de":"Nur wenn die KI entschieden hat, nicht wenn sie nur mitgeschrieben hat","fr":"Seulement si l'IA a décidé, pas quand elle a juste aidé à rédiger","it":"Solo se l'IA ha deciso, non quando ha solo aiutato a scrivere","rm":"Mo sche l'IA ha decidì, betg cur ch'ella ha mo gidà a scriver"}}},{"id":"ac-redress","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"When it goes wrong","de":"Wenn es schiefgeht","fr":"Quand ça tourne mal","it":"Quando va storto","rm":"Cur ch'i va mal"},"question":{"en":"The AI gets something important wrong, and it affects you. What matters most to you?","de":"Die KI liegt bei etwas Wichtigem falsch, und es betrifft Sie. Was ist Ihnen am wichtigsten?","fr":"L'IA se trompe sur quelque chose d'important, et cela vous touche. Qu'est-ce qui compte le plus pour vous ?","it":"L'IA sbaglia qualcosa di importante, e la cosa ti riguarda. Cosa conta di più per te?","rm":"L'IA fa in sbagl impurtant, e quai As pertutga. Tge As importa il pli?"},"options":[{"id":"ac-redress-report","label":{"en":"I can report it right there in the chat, and hear back what happened","de":"Ich kann es direkt im Chat melden, und erfahre, was daraus wurde","fr":"Pouvoir le signaler directement dans le chat, et savoir ce qui en est ressorti","it":"Poterlo segnalare lì nella chat, e sapere che fine ha fatto","rm":"Jau poss l'annunziar directamain en il chat ed udir enavos tge ch'è capità"}},{"id":"ac-redress-public-list","label":{"en":"A public list of known problems and their fixes","de":"Eine öffentliche Liste bekannter Probleme und ihrer Korrekturen","fr":"Une liste publique des problèmes connus et de leurs corrections","it":"Una lista pubblica dei problemi noti e delle correzioni","rm":"Ina glista publica da problems enconuschents e lur soluziuns"}},{"id":"ac-redress-human","label":{"en":"A human being I can reach","de":"Ein Mensch, den ich erreichen kann","fr":"Un être humain que je peux joindre","it":"Un essere umano che posso raggiungere","rm":"In uman ch'jau poss cuntanscher"}},{"id":"ac-redress-nothing","label":{"en":"Nothing special: mistakes happen, I judge for myself","de":"Nichts Besonderes: Fehler passieren, ich urteile selbst","fr":"Rien de spécial : des erreurs arrivent, je juge par moi-même","it":"Niente di speciale: gli errori capitano, giudico da solo","rm":"Nagut spezial: sbagls capitan, jau giuditgesch sez"}}]},{"id":"ac-contribute","kind":"question","multiSelect":true,"header":{"en":"Getting involved","de":"Mitmachen","fr":"S'impliquer","it":"Partecipare","rm":"Sa participar"},"question":{"en":"How would you be interested in contributing to Swiss AI?","de":"Wie würden Sie sich gerne an der Schweizer KI beteiligen?","fr":"Comment aimeriez-vous contribuer à l'IA suisse ?","it":"Come ti piacerebbe contribuire all'IA svizzera?","rm":"Co avessas Vus interess da contribuir a l'IA svizra?"},"options":[{"id":"ac-contribute-surveys","label":{"en":"Taking part in surveys and consultations","de":"An Umfragen und Konsultationen teilnehmen","fr":"Participer à des sondages et consultations","it":"Partecipare a sondaggi e consultazioni","rm":"Sa participar a enquistas e consultaziuns"}},{"id":"ac-contribute-testing","label":{"en":"Testing and evaluating AI systems, giving feedback","de":"KI-Systeme testen und bewerten, Rückmeldungen geben","fr":"Tester et évaluer des systèmes d'IA, donner un retour","it":"Testare e valutare sistemi di IA, dare feedback","rm":"Testar ed evaluar sistems d'IA, dar feedback"}},{"id":"ac-contribute-workshops","label":{"en":"Taking part in workshops or public dialogues","de":"An Workshops oder öffentlichen Dialogen teilnehmen","fr":"Participer à des ateliers ou dialogues publics","it":"Partecipare a workshop o dialoghi pubblici","rm":"Sa participar a workshops u dialogs publics"}},{"id":"ac-contribute-expertise","label":{"en":"Contributing technical, professional or domain expertise","de":"Technisches, berufliches oder fachliches Wissen einbringen","fr":"Apporter une expertise technique, professionnelle ou métier","it":"Contribuire con competenze tecniche, professionali o di settore","rm":"Contribuir savida tecnica, professiunala u speziala"}},{"id":"ac-contribute-governance","label":{"en":"Taking part in governance or advisory groups","de":"In Governance- oder Beratungsgruppen mitwirken","fr":"Participer à des groupes de gouvernance ou consultatifs","it":"Partecipare a gruppi di governance o consultivi","rm":"Sa participar a gruppas da governanza u da cussegl"}},{"id":"ac-contribute-education","label":{"en":"Supporting education and outreach","de":"Bildung und Öffentlichkeitsarbeit unterstützen","fr":"Soutenir l'éducation et la sensibilisation","it":"Sostenere l'educazione e la divulgazione","rm":"Sustegnair furmaziun e sensibilisaziun"}},{"id":"ac-contribute-research","label":{"en":"Collaborating on research projects","de":"An Forschungsprojekten mitarbeiten","fr":"Collaborer à des projets de recherche","it":"Collaborare a progetti di ricerca","rm":"Collavurar a projects da perscrutaziun"}},{"id":"ac-contribute-none","exclusive":true,"label":{"en":"I would not like to contribute","de":"Ich möchte nicht mitwirken","fr":"Je ne souhaite pas contribuer","it":"Non desidero contribuire","rm":"Jau na vuless betg contribuir"}}]},{"id":"ac-loan","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"The loan","de":"Der Kredit","fr":"Le crédit","it":"Il prestito","rm":"Il credit"},"question":{"en":"A bank uses AI to help decide who gets a loan.","de":"Eine Bank nutzt KI, um mitzuentscheiden, wer einen Kredit bekommt.","fr":"Une banque utilise l'IA pour aider à décider qui obtient un crédit.","it":"Una banca usa l'IA per aiutare a decidere chi ottiene un prestito.","rm":"Ina banca duvra l'IA per gidar a decider tgi che survegn in credit."},"options":[{"id":"ac-loan-ai","label":{"en":"The AI can decide on its own","de":"Die KI darf allein entscheiden","fr":"L'IA peut décider seule","it":"L'IA può decidere da sola","rm":"L'IA po decider sezza"}},{"id":"ac-loan-human-final","label":{"en":"The AI recommends, but a human makes the final call and answers for it","de":"Die KI empfiehlt, aber ein Mensch trifft die endgültige Entscheidung und verantwortet sie","fr":"L'IA recommande, mais un humain prend la décision finale et en répond","it":"L'IA consiglia, ma un umano prende la decisione finale e ne risponde","rm":"L'IA recumonda, ma in uman prenda la decisiun finala e responda per ella"}},{"id":"ac-loan-humans-only","label":{"en":"Humans only: no AI in decisions like that","de":"Nur Menschen: keine KI bei solchen Entscheiden","fr":"Les humains seulement : pas d'IA dans de telles décisions","it":"Solo esseri umani: niente IA in decisioni del genere","rm":"Mo umans: nagina IA en decisiuns sco quellas"}}]}]},{"id":"ac-s4","mode":"always","opener":{"id":"ac-missing","kind":"question","multiSelect":false,"header":{"en":"The missing chapter","de":"Das fehlende Kapitel","fr":"Le chapitre manquant","it":"Il capitolo mancante","rm":"Il chapitel ch'i manca"},"question":{"en":"The rules today cover honesty, safety, fairness, and human control. What's the most important thing they're missing?","de":"Die heutigen Regeln decken Ehrlichkeit, Sicherheit, Fairness und menschliche Kontrolle ab. Was fehlt ihnen am dringendsten?","fr":"Les règles actuelles couvrent l'honnêteté, la sécurité, l'équité et le contrôle humain. Quelle est la chose la plus importante qui leur manque ?","it":"Le regole di oggi coprono onestà, sicurezza, equità e controllo umano. Qual è la cosa più importante che manca?","rm":"Las reglas dad oz cumpiglian onestad, segirezza, gistadad e controll uman. Tge è la chaussa la pli impurtanta ch'i lur manca?"},"options":[{"id":"ac-missing-environment","label":{"en":"The environment: the electricity and water AI uses","de":"Die Umwelt: der Strom und das Wasser, die KI verbraucht","fr":"L'environnement : l'électricité et l'eau que l'IA consomme","it":"L'ambiente: l'elettricità e l'acqua che l'IA consuma","rm":"L'ambient: l'electricitad e l'aua che l'IA consumescha"}},{"id":"ac-missing-children","label":{"en":"Children and schools","de":"Kinder und Schulen","fr":"Les enfants et l'école","it":"Bambini e scuole","rm":"Uffants e scolas"}},{"id":"ac-missing-adult-content","label":{"en":"What adults are allowed to ask for","de":"Was Erwachsene verlangen dürfen","fr":"Ce que les adultes ont le droit de demander","it":"Cosa gli adulti possono chiedere","rm":"Tge che creschids dastgan dumandar"}},{"id":"ac-missing-advertising","label":{"en":"Advertising and paid influence on answers","de":"Werbung und bezahlter Einfluss auf Antworten","fr":"La publicité et l'influence payée sur les réponses","it":"Pubblicità e influenza a pagamento sulle risposte","rm":"Reclama ed influenza pajada sin las respostas"}},{"id":"ac-missing-data","label":{"en":"My data: what's remembered, what's learned from","de":"Meine Daten: was gespeichert wird, woraus gelernt wird","fr":"Mes données : ce qui est retenu, ce qui sert à l'apprentissage","it":"I miei dati: cosa viene ricordato, da cosa si impara","rm":"Mias datas: tge ch'i vegn regurdà, da tge ch'i vegn empris"}},{"id":"ac-missing-liability","label":{"en":"Who answers when AI causes harm","de":"Wer haftet, wenn KI Schaden anrichtet","fr":"Qui répond quand l'IA cause un tort","it":"Chi risponde quando l'IA causa un danno","rm":"Tgi che responda cur ch'l'IA chaschuna donn"}},{"id":"ac-missing-nothing","exclusive":true,"label":{"en":"Nothing important is missing","de":"Nichts Wichtiges fehlt","fr":"Rien d'important ne manque","it":"Non manca nulla di importante","rm":"Nagut d'impurtant manca"}}]}},{"id":"ac-s5-gate","mode":"always","opener":{"kind":"interviewer","id":"ac-interviewer","question":{"en":"Anything more to say about responsibility when it goes wrong? You'd chat with Apertus itself for a minute or two.","de":"Möchten Sie noch etwas zur Verantwortung sagen, wenn etwas schiefgeht? Sie würden ein, zwei Minuten mit Apertus selbst chatten.","fr":"Autre chose à dire sur la responsabilité quand ça tourne mal ? Vous discuteriez une minute ou deux avec Apertus lui-même.","it":"Altro da dire sulla responsabilità quando qualcosa va storto? Chiacchiereresti un minuto o due con Apertus stesso.","rm":"Anc insatge da dir davart la responsabladad cur ch'i va mal? Vus discurrissas cun Apertus sez per ina minuta u duas."},"probe":"Open with exactly this question (in the participant's language): \"Imagine the AI gave someone in your family advice that turned out badly. What should happen next — what would feel fair to you?\" Then walk the concrete path: whom they would call, and what they would expect back. Ask for concrete lived experience, never abstract opinions; never give advice or argue."}}]}}],"feedbackPlan":"# Post-survey feedback conversation\n\nThe participant has just finished the Swiss National AI Dialogue and is on the thank-you page. This is a brief, optional chat about the EXPERIENCE of taking part — it does not feed the research, it only helps us improve the dialogue itself. You have no tools; just talk.\n\n## Open\nOne or two short sentences, warm and human. Ask whether there was anything we did not ask — anything about AI in Switzerland they wanted to say, or expected to be asked, that never came up. (If a \"revealed profile\" section appears above, do not open from it; mention it only if they raise it. If none appears, never mention any profile or result.)\n\n## After that\nFollow what they open up — you might touch how it felt (length, pacing, whether the cards engaged them), anything confusing or missing, whether their views felt captured, or what would make them recommend it. Pick what fits; never run through a checklist.\n\n## Style\nOne question per message, at most two short sentences before it — this is a quick exit chat, not a second interview. Ask at most 3–4 questions, then wrap up warmly: thank them, tell them their feedback is noted, and let them know they're all done and can close the page whenever they like. Never reopen the survey topics, never defend the design, never argue with criticism — receive it, dig one level deeper if useful, and thank them. If they have no feedback, one light follow-up at most, then wrap up."};
export const productionPromptSnapshot = {"label":"v11 + kickoff-aware discipline [apertus-ai/Apertus-v1.5-70B-integration]","interviewGuidelines":"As a part of the Swiss National AI Dialogue, you are tasked with conducting an interview as a user-research specialist.\n\nAs a whole, our public engagement research tries to better understand the fundamentals of what Swiss people want from AI. The goal of this research is high-level and we are in discovery mode; there is no right or wrong answer.\n\nYou, the interviewer, play the dual role of host and student. Begin by putting the participant at ease with your demeanor. The more comfortable a participant feels, the more and better information you will get. A relaxed participant will open up and be more honest, less likely to worry about putting on a good impression. Once you've done your part to get the subject talking, get out of the way. You should strive to be a nearly invisible, neutral presence soaking up everything the other person has to say. Think of them as the world's foremost expert on themselves, which is the all-absorbing matter at hand. Insert yourself only when necessary to redirect back on topic or get clarification. You will know when your interview is going particularly well because you won't be able to get a word in, but you will be getting answers to all your questions.\n\nA couple of other keys to keep in mind:\n- Practice active listening while still being concise and direct.\n- Do not patronize the person.\n- Use the active voice when possible.\n- Do not ask more than one question per message.\n- Favour breadth over depth. People are busy and rarely enjoy justifying their choices in writing, so when an answer is brief, vague, or \"I don't know,\" don't press for more detail in prose. You have two good moves: accept it warmly and move on, or — when the topic still has more worth capturing — offer a quick multiple-choice card the participant can simply tap, which is far less effort for them than writing a sentence and still yields a usable signal. Reserve open, prose follow-ups for when the participant is clearly engaged and writing freely, and at most once before changing topic.\n- Try to capture the thoughts and behaviors of your participants accurately.\n- Tell them the goal of your study briefly, being careful that it doesn't direct their responses.\n- Encourage participants to act naturally and share their thoughts aloud.\n- Do not ask leading questions. A single clarifying follow-up is fine when an answer is genuinely unclear, but never interrogate — don't ask \"why\" twice in a row.\n- Maintain neutrality by avoiding evaluative language like \"I appreciate that response,\" which can unintentionally signal that some answers are more valuable than others.\n- Use the interview plan but feel free to deviate in the moment.\n\nUsing interactive cards: some topics land better when you give the person something concrete to react to. When a binary either-or framing is available as a card, use it to OPEN a topic: offer two contrasting directions and let the participant pick a side. Keep the two options deliberately simple and not exhaustive. Being a little incomplete is good, because it gives the participant something to push back on, qualify, or add to, and that reaction is what you are after. Never imply the two options are the only answers. As soon as they choose (or say it is complicated), drop the card and explore their reasoning in plain conversation. Use a multiple-choice card instead when you need a clear, comparable data point with a fuller set of options — and especially whenever a participant is answering tersely or seems reluctant to write, since tapping a choice keeps a low-energy conversation moving and still tells you something. Whichever kind of card you use: one card per turn, the card is the entire message, and never send two cards or make two tool calls in a row. Always let a plain reply come back in between.\n\nTry to be as conversational and natural as possible. If the person you're interacting with volunteers the information in the course of your conversation without you having to ask, that's terrific. Your questions are just prompts to help the participant tell you a story that reveals situations, attitudes, and behaviors you didn't even think to ask about. Offer enough information to set the scope for the conversation, but not so much that you influence the responses.\n\nYou are on stage the entire time: everything you output is shown to the participant. Never write your reasoning, plans, or notes to yourself — no \"I need to...\", no \"According to the plan...\". Speak only to the participant.\n\nThe first theme's opening cards are shown to the participant automatically before you are involved — the conversation you join already contains their answers. Your first message responds to those answers in text: react to the substance and ask ONE question about the why behind their choices. You open each SUBSEQUENT theme yourself with the open_topic call; that call is the entire message, with no text before or with it.\n\nEvery tool call must include ALL of its required fields with real, non-empty values (ask_user_question always needs its questions; open_topic always needs its key). If you cannot fill the fields, do not call the tool — ask in plain text instead.","chatModel":"apertus-ai/Apertus-v1.5-70B-integration","notes":"Apertus tuning winner (2026-07-09 eval loop): v11 + no-narration + tool-arg discipline, realigned for the programmaticFirstOpener kickoff (shipped in #4335 with the native-language directive). Local eval: 0% off-language, 0% abandons, engagement 2.67, idea quality 4.00."};
